#. Korean sky culture name
msgid "Korean"
msgstr "Coreano"

#. Korean sky culture introduction section in markdown format
msgid ""
"The *Cheonsang Yeolcha Bunyajido* (天象列次分野之圖, \"Chart of Constellations, Each"
" Star Division, and Their Field Allocations\") is one of the oldest and most"
" representative ancient star maps existing in Korea. It was first carved on "
"stone in 1396 AD (the 3rd year of King Taejo of the Joseon Dynasty), but its"
" original source can be traced back to the Unified Silla and Goryeo period, "
"and even directly to Chinese star charts from the Tang Dynasty (or earlier)."
" Today, it serves not only as an important physical artifact for studying "
"East Asian ancient astronomy, but also as a testament to the long-term "
"exchange and integration among East Asian countries in the fields of "
"astronomy, calendrics, and astrology."
msgstr ""
"O *Cheonsang Yeolcha Bunyajido* (天象列次分野之圖, \"Carta das constelacións, cada "
"división estelar e as súas asignacións de campo\") é un dos mapas estelares "
"antigos máis vellos e representativos que existen en Corea. Foi gravado en "
"pedra por primeira vez no ano 1396 d.C. (o terceiro ano do rei Taejo da "
"dinastía Joseon), pero a súa fonte orixinal remóntase ó período unificado de"
" Silla e Goryeo, e mesmo directamente ás cartas estelares chinesas da "
"dinastía Tang (ou anterior). Hoxe en día, serve non só como un importante "
"artefacto físico para estudar a astronomía antiga do leste asiático, senón "
"tamén como unha testemuña do intercambio e a integración a longo prazo entre"
" os países do leste asiático nos campos da astronomía, os calendarios e a "
"astroloxía."

#. Korean sky culture description section in markdown format
msgid ""
"![](illustrations/Cheonsang_yeolcha_bunyajido.jpg)\n"
"\n"
"*Rubbing of the Second Carving of the Cheonsang Yeolcha Bunyajido*\n"
"\n"
"The Chinese, Korean, and Japanese constellations have the same origin and look very similar in shape. The names of the constellations first appeared in the Records of the Grand Historian (史記) of the Western Han dynasty, which recorded more than 100 constellations before 100 BC. In the 3rd century AD, the constellations were standardized, eventually establishing 283 constellations with 1464 stars. During the Sui and Tang dynasties (7th-8th c. AD), Chinese astronomical works spread to Korea and Japan. Representative works from this period include the Dunhuang Star Map from China, the *Cheonsang Yeolcha Bunyajido* from Korea, and the Moon's path chart (格子月進図) from Japan. After the Tang dynasty, the star patterns of the three countries began to develop independently, and the *Cheonsang Yeolcha Bunyajido* became the representative star map of Korean constellations.\n"
"\n"
"### Historical Background\n"
"\n"
"According to the postscript at the bottom of the stone tablet, there was originally an astronomical map stone in Pyongyang, which sank into the Taedong River during a war, and its rubbings were gradually lost. Shortly after King Taejo (이성계, 李成桂) ascended the throne, someone presented a rubbing. The king regarded it as a great treasure and ordered the Office of Astronomical Observation (書雲觀) to re-carve a stone based on this rubbing. The office noted that the star positions had shifted due to precession and recommended re-measuring the meridian transit stars at dawn and dusk for different seasons to produce a new map. After the king's approval, the office submitted a new treatise *Jungseonggi* (中星記) in mid-1395, and then a new star map was carved on stone using the old chart and the newly measured stars. The inscription is dated \"December of the 28th year of the Hongwu era\", i.e., January 1396.\n"
"\n"
"This stone tablet has star maps and inscriptions on both sides, identical in content but upside down relative to each other. Side A has the star map at the top and the title/inscription below, shifted to one side and misaligned vertically. Side B has a typical layout (title, star map, inscription), but the figures and text are almost completely worn away. Various guesses exist about the reason for double-sided carving: scarcity of large stone, a re-carving during King Sejong or Sejo's reign, or even that Side A is a draft.\n"
"\n"
"By the reign of King Sukjong (1674-1720), the original stone was badly worn (another account says it was buried in ruins after the Japanese invasion of 1592-1598). In 1687 (13th year of Sukjong), a new stone was re-carved from rubbings and placed under a small shelter at the Royal Observatory outside Changdeokgung. The original is called \"First Carving\", and the new one \"Second Carving\". In 1770 (46th year of King Yeongjo), the First Carving was found at Gyeongbokgung; Yeongjo ordered it moved to the Royal Observatory to be kept together with the Second Carving, and named the storage place \"Geungyeongak\", inscribing the plaque with his own handwriting.\n"
"\n"
"After the fall of the Joseon Dynasty in 1910, Geungyeongak was destroyed, and both stones were left under the eaves of Myeongjeongjeon in Changgyeongwon (later renamed Changgyeongwon). In 1936, the American missionary W. C. Rufus praised the map in his book *Astronomy in Korea* as \"a detailed and accurate astronomical chart that is a compilation of Asian planetariums\", bringing the stones to world attention. After wars and turbulence, they returned to public view only in the 1960s, and were collected by museums in the 1970s. In 1985, the First Carving was designated as National Treasure No. 228 of Korea, and the Second Carving as Treasure No. 837. Both are now housed in the National Palace Museum of Korea next to Gyeongbokgung.\n"
"\n"
"### Content and Characteristics\n"
"\n"
"The Cheonsang Yeolcha Bunyajido depicts 1467 stars, a slight change from the traditional Chinese count of 1464: it adds one constellation \"Jongdaebu\" (宗大夫, 4 stars, e.g. 74 Oph) in the Heavenly Market Enclosure; adds one star to Munchang (文昌, e.g. τ UMa), one to Yeondo (輦道, e.g. 17 Cyg), and one to Cheonwon (天園, e.g. κ Eri); removes three stars from Gibu (器府, e.g. δ Cen); and omits the constelltion Cheongi (天記, 1 star, possibly γ Pyx). Some star names differ from common versions (e.g., Cheonchang \"天槍\" written as \"天倉\", Donggu \"東甌\" as \"東區\", Gyeonha \"梗河\" as \"更河\" with different characters, Jwagyeong/Ugyeong \"左/右更\" as \"左/右梗\" with different characters). In this sky culture, these errors have been corrected.\n"
"\n"
"Compared with the Suzhou Star Map and most traditional Chinese star maps, the *Cheonsang Yeolcha Bunyajido* has three notable features:\n"
"\n"
"1. Variable star sizes: Bright stars such as Sirius (Wolf), Canopus (Old Man), and Arcturus (Great Horn) are drawn significantly larger than others.\n"
"2. Labeling characteristics: Many constellations are labeled with their star counts, but important groups like the Northern Dipper and the walls of the Three Enclosures are not labeled.\n"
"3. Different connections and positions: The connection patterns and relative positions of some constellations differ markedly from the post-Song Dynasty Chinese tradition, largely because China continued frequent astronomical observations after the Song, leading to many changes in the constellations.\n"
"\n"
"### Astronomical Structure\n"
"\n"
"The *Cheonsang Yeolcha Bunyajido* belongs to the typical \"covering diagram\" (a representation under the gaitian cosmology). It features three concentric circles centered on the north celestial pole:\n"
"\n"
"- Inner circle (circumpolar circle / circle of perpetual apparition): The smallest circle; stars inside never set at the observing latitude.\n"
"- Equator: The middle circle.\n"
"- Outer circle (circle of perpetual occultation): The largest circle; stars outside never rise.\n"
"\n"
"In addition, a circle inclined 24° to the equator represents the ecliptic – the apparent path of the Sun. From the inner circle, 28 radial lines of unequal spacing correspond to the lunar mansion degree lines, with their values inscribed outside the outer circle, matching the Shi Shi's (石氏) degree values listed below.\n"
"\n"
"Outside the outer circle, there are texts for the twelve Earthly Branches, the twelve states/fields, and the twelve zodiacal signs. Above the map, surrounding the character \"天\" (heaven), are the dawn/dusk meridian stars for the 24 solar terms (as measured by the Office for the Jungseonggi). At the top left and right are the solar and lunar mansions, explaining the relationship between the Sun's motion and seasonal changes, the Moon's nine paths, and the nodes. Eight small patches contain the star counts, degrees, and configurations of the four directions' seven mansions each. On the lower side, the right section is \"On Heaven\" (mainly from the Book of Jin: Treatise on Astronomy, discussing the celestial sphere theory and other cosmologies), and the left section gives the Shi Shi's 28 mansion degree values and polar distances. The bottommost postscript records the origin of the carving, praises King Taejo, and lists the officials involved and the date.\n"
"\n"
"### Controversy over the Source Epoch\n"
"\n"
"The date of the original stone (the Pyongyang stone) on which the *Cheonsang Yeolcha Bunyajido* is based has long been a key question.\n"
"\n"
"W. C. Rufus believed the map came from Goguryeo and derived from a Chinese star chart of the year 672 AD (Xianheng 3rd year of Tang). This view was once widely accepted.\n"
"\n"
"Pan Nai, a Chinese historian of astronomy, argued from the positions of the equinoxes, relative positions of bright stars, and stars near the ecliptic and equator that the map must have been transmitted to Korea before the unification of Silla (675 AD), and that its source dates to the early Tang or earlier. He noted that the \"On Heaven\" text and the twelve divisions are quoted from the Book of Jin and Book of Sui (completed by Li Chunfeng in the mid-7th century), so the source cannot be earlier than that; but the lunar mansion degrees use the Shi Shi's values (observed around 100 BC) rather than Yi Xing's new measurements (early 8th century), so it cannot be later than Yi Xing. Thus the source map was drawn between the Zhenguan period and the early Kaiyuan period (ca. 627-713 AD).\n"
"\n"
"Additionally, the constellation \"Geonseong\" (建星, e.g. ξ2 Sgr) is carved as \"Ipseong\" (立星) on Side A of the First Carving (Side B is too worn), but restored to \"Geonseong\" on the Second Carving. This avoidance of the character \"建\" is thought to be a taboo for the name of Wang Geon (王建), the first king of the Goryeo Dynasty (Korean kings were posthumously tabooed). That suggests the source map came from the Goryeo period (918-1392), not Goguryeo. Early Joseon astronomers inherited many practices from Goryeo; if the original had no taboo, they would not have deliberately altered it, but if the original already had the taboo, they would naturally follow it.\n"
"\n"
"Taken together, a plausible reconstruction is that the map obtained by King Taejo was not a rubbing but a Goryeo copy. The copy changed \"Geonseong\" to \"Ipseong\" to avoid taboo, and when the First Carving was made, the Office followed that copy. Only later, for the Second Carving, was it changed back. Nevertheless, the star patterns and degree data retain early Tang to early Kaiyuan features, so the original source likely dates to the early 8th century or earlier.\n"
"\n"
"### Epoch of the Map\n"
"\n"
"The dating of the *Cheonsang Yeolcha Bunyajido* is complex. Its source may be Tang Chinese, but the data may be older. Most constellations indeed reflect early (pre-7th century) Chinese forms.\n"
"\n"
"However, mathematical calculations (e.g., Kim Dong-guk, 2020) show that different parts of the map yield different epochs. Roughly by polar distance: regions within 30° of the north celestial pole give an epoch around 1270 AD; the second group (45°-105°) around 240 AD; the third group (>105°) as early as 500 BC. The third group is problematic – Chinese constellations were not fully formed until the Han dynasty, and the earliest all-sky star catalog (Shi Shi's) dates only to around 100 BC. Moreover, historical records say the map was re-measured in 1395, yet the computed epochs never reach the 14th century.\n"
"\n"
"From the data, the lunar mansion degrees are Shi Shi's (ca. 100 BC), and many constellations correspond well to Shi Shi's data, but counterexamples exist. Some constellations are drawn differently from Chinese tradition, e.g., Cheongyun (天囷, e.g. α Cet) and Chilgong (七公, e.g. δ Boo). The constellations Gigwan (騎官, e.g. c1 Cen) and Urimgun (羽林軍, e.g. δ Aqr), which in Chinese tradition are described as \"three stars linked in groups of three\", are drawn as a single continuous chain in the Korean map. These details may indicate modifications between the Tang era and the 14th-century recarving.\n"
"\n"
"Re-examining the three groups: The first (polar region) clearly shows early Chinese shapes (pre-7th century) but enlarged. The map places star HIP 62572 at the north celestial pole – this star was closest to the pole in the 9th century, suggesting this region was adjusted (perhaps simply shifted and scaled) between the 7th and 14th centuries to put the new pole star at the center. The second group's computed date (3rd century AD) coincides with the time when Chen Zhuo Integrated the three star catalogs (including Shi Shi's) and standardized the 283 constellations. The third group's bizarre early date is likely due to large drawing errors and severe distortion near the map's periphery, making mathematical results unreliable.\n"
"\n"
"Overall, the *Cheonsang Yeolcha Bunyajido* has a very complex chronology. Its origins go back to Shi Shi's catalog (ca. 100 BC) and Chen Zhuo's standardization (3rd century AD), but later modifications are evident. Different regions have different epochs, indicating that the map was split and reassembled. Although it can be divided into three groups, the relative positions of constellations – for example, the obvious offset near the lunar mansion Jeo (氐宿, e.g. α2 Lib) – suggest that it may have undergone even more fragmentation. The method of reassembly was likely unscientific, resulting in different degrees of translation, rotation, and scaling in different regions of the map. Without considering these factors and preprocessing the data to correct such distortions, direct mathematical dating of the *Cheonsang Yeolcha Bunyajido* yields results that may contain significant errors.\n"
"\n"
"### Details Found During Identification\n"
"\n"
"Some small details were noticed during the identification. Though isolated and inconclusive, they may still be worth noting for future research.\n"
"\n"
"For example, Buyeol (傅說, G Sco) and Eo (魚, M7) have polar distances >105° (third group). In both the Korean map and Shi Shi's catalog, Buyeol is placed north of Eo, which contradicts the actual relative positions. This consistency in error may indicate a direct data inheritance from Shi Shi.\n"
"\n"
"Conversely, there are also mismatches: Daereung (大陵) and Cheonseon (天船) (second group) – in Shi Shi's catalog, the northern stars are η Per and k Per, which do not match the Korean map; the only ancient Chinese record that matches the Korean map is a star catalog compiled during the Jingyou era of the Northern Song dynasty (1034 AD).\n"
"\n"
"Proper motion also affects shapes: η Cas in Wangnyang (王良) and λ Aur in Hamji (咸池) have positions in the Korean map that fit a later epoch rather than an early one; while ο2 Eri in Gujusugu (九州殊口) shows an early shape, though its identification is doubtful.\n"
"\n"
"Some scholars argue that such small details are insufficient to draw conclusions, given the map's inherent inaccuracy.\n"
"\n"
"### Identification of the Constellations\n"
"\n"
"Like the dating, the identification of the Korean map's stars is difficult and has no single accepted result.\n"
"\n"
"Because the map was likely split and reassembled, we must correctly assign each constellation to its original block, as positions shift between blocks. The constellations are highly consistent with early Chinese constellations, requiring deep familiarity with ancient Chinese star names. Moreover, because the map may have been modified several times between the Tang dynasty and the 14th century, one must also consider historical changes in Chinese constellations to decide which may have been altered. Later modifications can cause more serious problems: if carelessly done at that time, altered constellations might overlap with others; if many such overlaps exist, identification becomes extremely difficult.\n"
"\n"
"Our identification aims to reflect the original appearance of the Korean map. We fully considered historical changes. When choosing between shape and brightness, we gave priority to shape and position, even if that meant using fainter stars. In extreme cases, stars fainter than magnitude 6.5 had to be used – probably due to inaccuracies in the map rather than intentional choice. We did not directly assume that constellations overlap; however, when no other explanation was possible, we had to present them as overlapping (e.g., Gigwan 騎官 and Guyu 九斿).\n"
"\n"
"### Note on Constellation IDs for East Asian Sky Cultures\n"
"\n"
"China, Japan, and Korea share the same constellation system. The Chinese characters used for constellation names are largely identical, but their English translations differ, and the pronunciations in each language are completely different. Given the unique consistency of East Asian sky cultures, it is necessary to have an identical field as a primary key to identify the same constellation across different cultures. This will facilitate further comparative cultural research based on Stellarium.\n"
"\n"
"According to Stellarium's specification, constellation IDs (Abbreviated names) should use pronunciation-based abbreviations for ease of memorization, rather than plain numbers. However, as noted above, using a numeric ID as a common primary key across East Asian sky cultures is a more suitable choice. Therefore, we have decided to use numeric IDs instead of pronunciation-based abbreviations — not only because pronunciations vary across regions, but also because a dedicated `pronounce` field already exists, so there is no need for a redundant ID that reflects pronunciation.\n"
"\n"
"The order of constellation IDs in the current East Asian sky culture is derived from the Tang-Dynasty Chinese constellation poem Bu Tian Ge (Song of the Sky Pacers). This poem is widely known, and the constellation sequence it records is regarded as a conventional standard. Specifically, all 283 constellations are divided into 31 groups based on the Three Enclosures and the 28 Mansions. The Three Enclosures each use an initial letter (P, S, H) as a prefix, followed by numbers for the constellations within each Enclosure. Here P stands for the Purple Forbidden Enclosure, S for the Supreme Palace Enclosure, and H for the Heavenly Market Enclosure. In contrast, the 28 Mansions are numbered from 01 to 28, and the constellations within each mansion are named with letters. For example, 01A denotes the first constellation of the Horn Mansion."
msgstr ""
"![](illustrations/Cheonsang_yeolcha_bunyajido.jpg)\n"
"\n"
"*Calcado do segundo gravado do Cheonsang Yeolcha Bunyajido*\n"
"\n"
"As constelacións chinesa, coreana e xaponesa teñen a mesma orixe e teñen unha forma moi semellante. Os nomes das constelacións apareceron por primeira vez nos Rexistros do Gran Historiador (史記) da dinastía Han Occidental, que rexistraron máis de 100 constelacións antes do 100 a.C. No século III d.C., as constelacións foron estandarizadas, chegando finalmente a establecerse 283 constelacións con 1464 estrelas. Durante as dinastías Sui e Tang (s. VII-VIII d. C.), as obras astronómicas chinesas estendéronse por Corea e Xapón. Obras representativas deste período inclúen o mapa estelar de Dunhuang de China, o *Cheonsang Yeolcha Bunyajido* de Corea e a gráfica do camiño da Lúa (格子月進図) de Xapón. Despois da dinastía Tang, os patróns de estrelas dos tres países comezaron a desenvolverse de forma independente e o *Cheonsang Yeolcha Bunyajido* converteuse no mapa estelar representativo das constelacións coreanas.\n"
"\n"
"### Antecedentes históricos\n"
"\n"
"Segundo a posdata na parte inferior da taboíña de pedra, orixinalmente había unha pedra de mapa astronómico en Pyongyang, que afundiu no río Taedong durante unha guerra, e os seus trazos fóronse perdendo gradualmente. Pouco despois de que o rei Taejo (이성계, 李成桂) subise ó trono, alguén presentou un gravado. O rei considerouno como un gran tesouro e ordenou á Oficina de Observación Astronómica (書雲觀) tallar de novo unha pedra a partir deste gravado. A oficina observou que as posicións das estrelas cambiaran debido á precesión e recomendou volver medir os meridianos das estrelas de tránsito ó amencer e ó solpor durante diferentes estacións para producir un novo mapa. Despois da aprobación do rei, a oficina presentou un novo tratado *Jungseonggi* (中星記) a mediados de 1395, e despois un novo mapa estelar foi tallado na pedra usando a antiga carta e as estrelas recentemente medidas. A inscrición está datada \"Decembro do ano 28 da era Hongwu\", é dicir, xaneiro de 1396.\n"
"\n"
"Esta taboíña de pedra ten mapas de estrelas e inscricións nos dous lados, de contido idéntico pero boca abaixo entre si. O lado A ten o mapa de estrelas na parte superior e o título/inscrición abaixo, desprazado a un lado e desalineado verticalmente. A cara B ten un esquema típico (título, mapa de estrelas, inscrición), pero as figuras e o texto están case completamente desgastados. Existen varias suposicións sobre o motivo da talla a dobre cara: escaseza de pedra grande, unha nova durante o reinado do rei Sejong ou Sejo, ou mesmo que a cara A é un borrador.\n"
"\n"
"Durante o reinado do rei Sukjong (1674-1720), a pedra orixinal estaba moi gastada (outro relato di que foi enterrada en ruínas despois da invasión xaponesa de 1592-1598). En 1687 (ano 13 de Sukjong), unha nova pedra foi tallada de novo a partir de calcos e colocada baixo un pequeno abrigo no Observatorio Real fóra de Changdeokgung. O orixinal chámase \"Primeira Talla\" e a nova \"Segunda Talla\". En 1770 (ano 46 do rei Yeongjo), a primeira escultura foi atopada en Gyeongbokgung; Yeongjo ordenou que a trasladasen ó Observatorio Real para manterse xunto coa Segunda Escultura, e chamou ó lugar de almacenamento \"Geungyeongak\", inscribindo a placa coa súa propia caligrafía.\n"
"\n"
"Despois da caída da dinastía Joseon en 1910, Geungyeongak foi destruído, e ambas pedras quedaron ó abeiro de Myeongjeongjeon en Changgyeongwon (logo renomeado como Changgyeongwon). En 1936, o misioneiro estadounidense W. C. Rufus eloxiou o mapa no seu libro *Astronomía en Corea* como \"unha carta astronómica detallada e precisa que é unha compilación de planetarios asiáticos\", chamando as pedras á atención mundial. Despois de guerras e turbulencias, volveron á vista pública só nos anos 60 e foron recollidas polos museos na década de 1970. En 1985, a Primeira Talla foi designada como Tesouro Nacional No 228 de Corea, e a Segunda Talla como Tesouro no 837. Ambas agora están aloxadas no Museo do Palacio Nacional de Corea xunto a Gyeongbokgung.\n"
"\n"
"### Contido e características\n"
"\n"
"O Cheonsang Yeolcha Bunyajido representa 1467 estrelas, unha lixeira variación con respecto á conta tradicional chinesa de 1464: engade unha constelación de \"Jongdaebu\" (宗大夫, 4 estrelas, por exemplo, 74 Oph) no Recinto do Mercado Celestial; engade unha estrela a Munchang (文昌, por exemplo, τ UMa), unha a Yeondo (輦道, por exemplo, 17 Cyg) e unha a Cheonwon (天園, por exemplo, κ Eri); elimina tres estrelas de Gibu (器府, por exemplo, δ Cen); e omite a constelación de Cheongi (天記, 1 estrela, posiblemente γ Pyx). Algúns nomes de estrelas difiren das versións habituais (por exemplo, Cheonchang \"天槍\" escrito como \"天倉\", Donggu \"東甌\" como \"東區\", Gyeonha \"梗河\" como \"更河\" con caracteres diferentes, Jwagyeong/Ugyeong \"左/右更\" como \"左/右梗\" con caracteres diferentes). Nesta cultura do ceo, estes erros foron corrixidos.\n"
"\n"
"En comparación co mapa estelar de Suzhou e a maioría dos mapas estelares chineses tradicionais, o *Cheonsang Yeolcha Bunyajido* ten tres características notables:\n"
"\n"
"1. Tamaños variables das estrelas: as estrelas brillantes como Sirio (Lobo), Canopus (Home Vello) e Arcturus (Gran Corno) debuxanse significativamente máis grandes ca outras.\n"
"\n"
"2. Características da etiquetaxe: moitas constelacións están etiquetadas co seu número de estrelas, pero grupos importantes como o Carro Setentrional e as paredes dos Tres Recintos non o están.\n"
"\n"
"3. Diferentes conexións e posicións: os patróns de conexión e as posicións relativas dalgunhas constelacións difiren notablemente da tradición chinesa posterior á dinastía Song, en gran parte porque China continuou con frecuentes observacións astronómicas despois da dinastía Song, o que levou a moitos cambios nas constelacións.\n"
"\n"
"### Estrutura astronómica\n"
"\n"
"O *Cheonsang Yeolcha Bunyajido* pertence ó típico \"diagrama de cobertura\" (unha representación baixo a cosmoloxía gaitiana). Presenta tres círculos concéntricos centrados no polo norte celeste:\n"
"\n"
"- Círculo interior (círculo circumpolar / círculo de aparición perpetua): o círculo máis pequeno; as estrelas do interior nunca se poñen na latitude de observación.\n"
"- Ecuador: o círculo central.\n"
"- Círculo exterior (círculo de ocultación perpetua): o círculo máis grande; as estrelas do exterior nunca saen.\n"
"\n"
"Ademais, un círculo inclinado 24° respecto ó ecuador representa a eclíptica, a traxectoria aparente do Sol. Desde o círculo interior, 28 liñas radiais de espazado desigual corresponden ás liñas de graos da mansión lunar, cos seus valores inscritos fóra do círculo exterior, coincidindo cos valores de graos de Shi Shi (石氏) que se enumeran a continuación.\n"
"\n"
"Fóra do círculo exterior, hai textos para as doce Ramas Terrestres, os doce estados/campos e os doce signos zodiacais. Enriba do mapa, arredor do carácter \"天\" (ceo), están as estrelas do meridiano do amencer/solpor para os 24 termos solares (segundo as medidas da Oficina do Jungseonggi). Na parte superior esquerda e dereita están as mansións solares e lunares, que explican a relación entre o movemento do Sol e os cambios estacionais, as nove traxectorias da Lúa e os nodos. Oito pequenas zonas conteñen o número de estrelas, os graos e as configuracións das sete mansións das catro direccións cada unha. Na parte inferior, a sección dereita é \"Sobre o ceo\" (principalmente do Libro de Jin: Tratado de astronomía, que trata a teoría da esfera celeste e outras cosmoloxías), e a sección esquerda dá os valores dos 28 graos das mansións e as distancias polares de Shi Shi. A posdata inferior rexistra a orixe da talla, eloxia o rei Taejo e enumera os funcionarios implicados e a data.\n"
"\n"
"### Controversia sobre a época orixinal\n"
"\n"
"A data da pedra orixinal (a pedra de Pyongyang) na que se basea o *Cheonsang Yeolcha Bunyajido* foi durante moito tempo unha cuestión clave.\n"
"\n"
"W. C. Rufus cría que o mapa proviña de Goguryeo e derivaba dunha carta estelar chinesa do ano 672 d.C. (Xianheng, terceiro ano do reinado Tang). Esta opinión foi amplamente aceptada noutro tempo.\n"
"\n"
"Pan Nai, un historiador chinés da astronomía, argumentou, a partir das posicións dos equinoccios, as posicións relativas das estrelas brillantes e as estrelas preto da eclíptica e o ecuador, que o mapa debeu ser transmitido a Corea antes da unificación de Silla (675 d.C.) e que a súa fonte data de principios do reinado Tang ou antes. Sinalou que o texto \"Sobre o ceo\" e as doce divisións están citadas do Libro de Jin e do Libro de Sui (completados por Li Chunfeng a mediados do século VII), polo que a fonte non pode ser anterior a iso; mais os graos da mansión lunar usan os valores de Shi Shi (observados arredor do ano 100 a. C.) en lugar das novas medidas de Yi Xing (principios do século VIII), polo que non pode ser posterior a Yi Xing. Polo tanto, o mapa orixinal foi debuxado entre o período Zhenguan e o período Kaiyuan temperán (aprox. 627-713 d. C.).\n"
"\n"
"Ademais, a constelación \"Geonseong\" (建星, por exemplo, ξ2 Sgr) está gravada como \"Ipseong\" (立星) na cara A da primeira talla (a cara B está demasiado desgastada), mais foi restaurada como \"Geonseong\" na segunda talla. Crese que evitar o carácter \"建\" é un tabú para o nome de Wang Geon (王建), o primeiro rei da dinastía Goryeo (os reis coreanos foron tabulados postumamente). Iso suxire que o mapa orixinal provén do período Goryeo (918-1392), non do Goguryeo. Os primeiros astrónomos de Joseon herdaron moitas prácticas de Goryeo; se o orixinal non tivese tabú, non o terían alterado deliberadamente, pero se o orixinal xa tivese o tabú, seguiríano naturalmente.\n"
"\n"
"En conxunto, unha reconstrución plausible é que o mapa obtido polo rei Taejo non era un calco, senón unha copia de Goryeo. A copia cambiou \"Geonseong\" por \"Ipseong\" para evitar o tabú, e cando se fixo a Primeira Talla, a Oficina seguiu esa copia. Só máis tarde, para a Segunda Talla, se volveu cambiar. Non obstante, os patróns estelares e os datos de graos conservan características desde a época Tang temperá ata a época Kaiyuan temperá, polo que a fonte orixinal probablemente data de principios do século VIII ou antes.\n"
"\n"
"### Época do Mapa\n"
"\n"
"A datación do *Cheonsang Yeolcha Bunyajido* é complexa. A súa fonte pode ser a chinesa Tang, pero os datos poden ser máis antigos. A maioría das constelacións reflicten formas chinesas temperás (antes do século VII).\n"
"\n"
"Non obstante, os cálculos matemáticos (por exemplo, Kim Dong-guk, 2020) mostran que as diferentes partes do mapa se producen en diferentes épocas. Aproximadamente pola distancia polar: as rexións dentro dos 30° do polo norte celeste dan unha época arredor do 1270 d.C.; o segundo grupo (45°-105°) arredor do 240 d.C.; o terceiro grupo (>105°) xa no 500 a.C. O terceiro grupo é problemático: as constelacións chinesas non se formaron completamente ata a dinastía Han, e o catálogo de estrelas de todo o ceo máis antigo (Shi Shi) data só de arredor do 100 a.C. Ademais, os rexistros históricos din que o mapa foi medido de novo en 1395, pero as épocas calculadas nunca chegan ó século XIV.\n"
"\n"
"Segundo os datos, os graos da mansión lunar son os de Shi Shi (ca. 100 a. C.) e moitas constelacións correspóndense ben cos datos de Shi Shi, pero existen contraexemplos. Algunhas constelacións debúxanse de forma diferente á tradición chinesa, por exemplo, Cheongyun (天囷, por exemplo, α Cet) e Chilgong (七公, por exemplo, δ Boo). As constelacións Gigwan (騎官, por exemplo, c1 Cen) e Urimgun (羽林軍, por exemplo, δ Aqr), que na tradición chinesa se describen como \"tres estrelas unidas en grupos de tres\", debúxanse como unha única cadea continua no mapa coreano. Estes detalles poden indicar modificacións entre a era Tang e a reedición do século XIV.\n"
"\n"
"Reexaminando os tres grupos: o primeiro (rexión polar) mostra claramente formas chinesas temperás (antes do século VII) pero ampliadas. O mapa sitúa a estrela HIP 62572 no polo norte celeste; esta estrela estaba máis preto do polo no século IX, o que suxire que esta rexión foi axustada (quizais simplemente desprazada e escalada) entre os séculos VII e XIV para colocar a nova estrela polar no centro. A data calculada do segundo grupo (século III d.C.) coincide co momento en que Chen Zhuo integrou os tres catálogos de estrelas (incluído o de Shi Shi) e estandarizou as 283 constelacións. A estraña data temperá do terceiro grupo probablemente se deba a grandes erros de debuxo e a unha grave distorsión preto da periferia do mapa, o que fai que os resultados matemáticos non sexan fiables.\n"
"\n"
"En xeral, o *Cheonsang Yeolcha Bunyajido* ten unha cronoloxía moi complexa. As súas orixes remóntanse ó catálogo de Shi Shi (ca. 100 a.C.) e á estandarización de Chen Zhuo (século III d.C.), pero son evidentes modificacións posteriores. As diferentes rexións teñen diferentes épocas, o que indica que o mapa foi dividido e reensamblado. Aínda que se pode dividir en tres grupos, as posicións relativas das constelacións (por exemplo, o evidente desprazamento preto da mansión lunar Jeo (氐宿, por exemplo, α2 Lib)) suxiren que puido sufrir aínda máis fragmentación. O método de remontaxe probablemente non foi científico, o que resultou en diferentes graos de translación, rotación e escala en diferentes rexións do mapa. Sen ter en conta estes factores e preprocesar os datos para corrixir tales distorsións, a datación matemática directa do *Cheonsang Yeolcha Bunyajido* produce resultados que poden conter erros significativos.\n"
"\n"
"### Detalles atopados durante a identificación\n"
"\n"
"Observáronse algúns pequenos detalles durante a identificación. Aínda que illados e pouco concluíntes, poden ser dignos de mención para futuras investigacións.\n"
"\n"
"Por exemplo, Buyeol (傅說, G Sco) e Eo (魚, M7) teñen distancias polares >105° (terceiro grupo). Tanto no mapa coreano como no catálogo de Shi Shi, Buyeol sitúase ó norte de Eo, o que contradí as posicións relativas reais. Esta coherencia no erro pode indicar unha herdanza directa de datos de Shi Shi.\n"
"\n"
"Pola contra, tamén hai discrepancias: Daereung (大陵) e Cheonseon (天船) (segundo grupo): no catálogo de Shi Shi, as estrelas setentrionais son η Per e k Per, que non coinciden co mapa coreano; o único rexistro chinés antigo que coincide co mapa coreano é un catálogo de estrelas compilado durante a era Jingyou da dinastía Song do Norte (1034 d.C.).\n"
"\n"
"O movemento propio tamén afecta ás formas: η Cas en Wangnyang (王良) e λ Aur en Hamji (咸池) teñen posicións no mapa coreano que se axustan a unha época posterior en lugar dunha temperá; mentres que ο2 Eri en Gujusugu (九州殊口) mostra unha forma temperá, aínda que a súa identificación é dubidosa.\n"
"\n"
"Algúns estudosos argumentan que detalles tan pequenos son insuficientes para sacar conclusións, dada a inexactitude inherente do mapa.\n"
"\n"
"### Identificación das constelacións\n"
"\n"
"Do mesmo xeito que a datación, a identificación das estrelas do mapa coreano é difícil e non ten un único resultado aceptado.\n"
"\n"
"Debido a que o mapa probablemente foi dividido e reensamblado, debemos asignar correctamente cada constelación ó seu bloque orixinal, xa que as posicións cambian entre os bloques. As constelacións son moi consistentes coas primeiras constelacións chinesas, o que require unha profunda familiaridade cos nomes das estrelas chinesas antigas. Ademais, dado que o mapa pode ter sido modificado varias veces entre a dinastía Tang e o século XIV, tamén hai que ter en conta os cambios históricos nas constelacións chinesas para decidir cales puideron ser alteradas. As modificacións posteriores poden causar problemas máis graves: se se fan descoidadamente nese momento, as constelacións alteradas poden solaparse con outras; se existen moitas desas superposicións, a identificación faise extremadamente difícil.\n"
"\n"
"A nosa identificación ten como obxectivo reflectir o aspecto orixinal do mapa coreano. Consideramos plenamente os cambios históricos. Ó elixirmos entre a forma e o brillo, demos prioridade á forma e á posición, aínda que iso significase usar estrelas máis tenues. En casos extremos, tiveron que usarse estrelas de magnitude inferior a 6,5, probablemente debido a inexactitudes no mapa en lugar de por unha elección intencionada. Non asumimos directamente que as constelacións se solapan; non obstante, cando non era posible outra explicación, tivemos que presentalas como superpostas (por exemplo, Gigwan 騎官 e Guyu 九斿).\n"
"\n"
"### Nota sobre os ID de constelacións para as culturas do ceo do leste asiático\n"
"\n"
"China, Xapón e Corea comparten o mesmo sistema de constelacións. Os caracteres chineses empregados para os nomes das constelacións son en gran parte idénticos, pero as súas traducións ó galego difiren e as pronuncias en cada idioma son completamente diferentes. Dada a consistencia única das culturas do ceo do leste asiático, é necesario ter un campo idéntico como clave primaria para identificar a mesma constelación en diferentes culturas. Isto facilitará unha maior investigación cultural comparativa baseada en Stellarium.\n"
"\n"
"Segundo a especificación de Stellarium, os ID de constelacións (nomes abreviados) deben usar abreviaturas baseadas na pronuncia para facilitar a memorización, en lugar de números simples. Non obstante, como se indicou anteriormente, usar un ID numérico como clave primaria común en todas as culturas do ceo do leste asiático é unha opción máis axeitada. Polo tanto, decidimos usar ID numéricos en lugar de abreviaturas baseadas na pronuncia, non só porque as pronuncias varían segundo as rexións, senón tamén porque xa existe un campo dedicado á \"pronuncia\", polo que non hai necesidade dun ID redundante que reflicta a pronuncia.\n"
"\n"
"A orde dos identificadores de constelacións na cultura celeste actual do leste asiático deriva do poema de constelacións chinés da dinastía Tang Bu Tian Ge (Canción dos Pasadores do Ceo). Este poema é amplamente coñecido e a secuencia de constelacións que rexistra considérase un estándar convencional. Especificamente, as 283 constelacións divídense en 31 grupos baseados nos Tres Recintos e as 28 Mansións. Os Tres Recintos usan unha letra inicial (P, S, H) como prefixo, seguida de números para as constelacións dentro de cada Recinto. Aquí P representa o Recinto Púrpura Prohibido, S o Recinto do Palacio Supremo e H o Recinto do Mercado Celestial. Pola contra, as 28 Mansións están numeradas do 01 ó 28 e as constelacións dentro de cada mansión noméanse con letras. Por exemplo, 01A denota a primeira constelación da Mansión do Corno."

#. Description of Korean constellation Purple Forbidden Palace
msgid ""
"*Purple Forbidden Enclosure* (Korean: 자미, Hanja: 紫微, Romanization: Jami) is "
"the place where the Heavenly Emperor resides and discusses affairs with "
"close ministers."
msgstr ""
"O *Recinto Prohibido Púrpura* (en coreano: 자미, en hanja: 紫微, romanizado: "
"Jami) é o lugar onde reside o Emperador Celestial e discute asuntos cos seus"
" ministros próximos."

#. Description of Korean constellation Northern Pole
msgid ""
"*Northern Pole* (Korean: 북극, Hanja: 北極, Romanization: Bukgeuk) consists of 5 stars in the central part of the *Purple Forbidden Enclosure*. It is one of the most important constellations in Chinese star culture. The five stars are *Crown Prince* (γ UMi), *Emperor* (β UMi), *Bastard* (4 UMi), *Harem* (3 UMi), and *Northern Pole* star (HIP 62572, also known as *Celestial Pivot* or *Ancient Star*).\n"
"\n"
"Due to precession, the Emperor Star (β UMi) was the brightest star closest to the north celestial pole for a long period before the Common Era, making it the North Star at that time. This period was crucial for the formation of the star official system, so this star held a lofty status and was regarded as the Celestial Emperor. The three stars around the Emperor Star (γ UMi, 4 UMi, 3 UMi) were seen as the *Three Excellencies* assisting the Celestial Emperor, which were the three highest-ranking officials in ancient times.\n"
"\n"
"Starting from the Han Dynasty, the north celestial pole gradually moved away from the Emperor Star and approached the faint star HIP 65595. This was the era when Chinese constellations were finally established. HIP 65595 was considered the North Star at that time, and together with the aforementioned *Emperor Star* and the *Three Excellencies*, a total of five stars formed the *Northern Pole* constellation. The meaning of the star officials was also reconstructed, with the *Three Excellencies* becoming *Crown Prince*, *Bastard*, and *Harem*.\n"
"\n"
"Soon, before the Sui and Tang Dynasties, the north celestial pole approached HIP 62572. This star is also faint but brighter than HIP 65595, so HIP 62572 replaced the previous HIP 65595 and became the new North Star. For several hundred years thereafter, spanning important dynasties such as Sui, Tang, Song, and Yuan, up to the Ming Dynasty when the *Xianglin* star chart was drawn, this star was observed as the North Star in China.\n"
"\n"
"In the Ming Dynasty, the north celestial pole moved away from HIP 62572 and approached α UMi, which is the contemporary North Star. However, since α UMi, as the brightest star in the *Gou Chen* constellation, already had a meaning that had been used for millennia, it could not be included as a member of the North Star official. Therefore, HIP 62572 continued to retain its name as *Northern Pole* *Celestial Pivot*, even though it was no longer the North Star."
msgstr ""
"*Polo Norte* (en coreano: 북극, en hanja: 北極, romanizado: Bukgeuk) consta de 5 estrelas na parte central do *Recinto Púrpura Prohibido*. É unha das constelacións máis importantes da cultura estelar chinesa. As cinco estrelas son *Príncipe Herdeiro* (γ UMi), *Emperador* (β UMi), *Bastardo* (4 UMi), *Harén* (3 UMi) e a estrela do *Polo Norte* (HIP 62572, tamén coñecida como *Pivote Celestial* ou *Estrela Antiga*).\n"
"\n"
"Debido á precesión, a Estrela Emperador (β UMi) foi a estrela brillante máis próxima ó polo norte celeste durante un longo período anterior á Era Común, o que a converteu na Estrela Polar naquel momento. Este período foi crucial para a formación do sistema oficial de estrelas, polo que esta estrela tivo un status elevado e foi considerada o Emperador Celestial. As tres estrelas arredor da Estrela Emperador (γ UMi, 4 UMi, 3 UMi) eran vistas como as *Tres Excelencias* que axudaban o Emperador Celestial, que eran os tres funcionarios de maior rango na antigüidade.\n"
"\n"
"A partir da dinastía Han, o polo norte celeste afastouse gradualmente da Estrela Emperador e achegouse á débil estrela HIP 65595. Esta foi a época na que se estableceron finalmente as constelacións chinesas. A HIP 65595 considerábase a Estrela Polar naquel momento e, xunto coa xa mencionada *Estrela Emperador* e as *Tres Excelencias*, un total de cinco estrelas formaban a constelación do *Polo Norte*. Tamén se reconstruíu o significado dos funcionarios das estrelas, e as *Tres Excelencias* convertéronse en *Príncipe Herdeiro*, *Bastardo* e *Harén*.\n"
"\n"
"Pouco despois, antes das dinastías Sui e Tang, o polo norte celeste achegouse a HIP 62572. Esta estrela tamén é tenue pero máis brillante ca HIP 65595, polo que HIP 62572 substituíu a anterior HIP 65595 e converteuse na nova Estrela Polar. Durante varios centos de anos despois, abarcando importantes dinastías como Sui, Tang, Song e Yuan, ata a dinastía Ming, cando se elaborou a carta estelar *Xianglin*, esta estrela observouse como a Estrela Polar na China.\n"
"\n"
"Na dinastía Ming, o polo norte celeste afastouse de HIP 62572 e achegouse a α UMi, que é a Estrela Polar contemporánea. Non obstante, dado que α UMi, como a estrela máis brillante da constelación *Gou Chen*, xa tiña un significado que se usara durante milenios, non se puido incluír como membro oficial da Estrela Polar. Polo tanto, HIP 62572 continuou a conservar o seu nome como *Polo Norte* *Pivote Celeste*, aínda que xa non era a Estrela Polar."

#. Description of Korean constellation Four Advisors
msgid ""
"*Four Advisors* (Korean: 사보, Hanja: 四輔, Romanization: Sabo) consists of 4 stars surrounding the *Northern Pole* star (HIP 62572). They represent four auxiliary ministers assisting the *Northern Pole*.\n"
"\n"
"Because the *Northern Pole* star has undergone positional changes from HIP 65595 to HIP 62572, the *Four Advisors* had to change accordingly, making the identification of these four stars on star charts often very difficult, and there can be significant differences between different star charts."
msgstr ""
"Os *Catro Conselleiros* (en coreano: 사보, en hanja: 四輔, romanizado: Sabo) constan de catro estrelas que rodean a estrela do *Polo Norte* (HIP 62572). Representan catro ministros auxiliares que axudan o *Polo Norte*.\n"
"\n"
"Dado que a estrela do *Polo Norte* sufriu cambios de posición desde HIP 65595 ata HIP 62572, os *Catro Conselleiros* tiveron que cambiar en consecuencia, o que fai que a identificación destas catro estrelas nas cartas estelares sexa a miúdo moi difícil, e pode haber diferenzas significativas entre as diferentes cartas estelares."

#. Description of Korean constellation Curved Array
msgid ""
"*Curved Array* (Korean: 구진, Hanja: 勾陳, Romanization: Gujin) consists of 6 stars in the *Purple Forbidden Enclosure*, arranged like a hook. It represents the Emperor's harem, with the brightest star α UMi representing the primary consort.\n"
"\n"
"During the Han Dynasty, *Curved Array* consisted of 4 stars (α, δ, ε, ζ). Later, no later than the Jin Dynasty, two stars were added (HIP 16489, HIP 4283). Because the two newly added stars at the hook's head were too faint, its shape frequently changed on star charts. Since the Song Dynasty, it was fixed as 2 UMi and HIP 112833. Later, due to positional changes of the *Interior Seats of the Five Emperors*, during the Yuan and Ming Dynasties, HIP 112833 was replaced by HIP 113116."
msgstr ""
"*Matriz Curva* (en coreano: 구진, hanja: 勾陳, romanizado: Gujin) consta de 6 estrelas no *Recinto Púrpura Prohibido*, dispostas como un gancho. Representa o harén do emperador, coa estrela máis brillante α UMi representando a consorte principal.\n"
"\n"
"Durante a dinastía Han, *Matriz Curva* constaba de 4 estrelas (α, δ, ε, ζ). Máis tarde, non máis tarde cá dinastía Jin, engadíronse dúas estrelas (HIP 16489, HIP 4283). Debido a que as dúas estrelas recentemente engadidas na cabeza do gancho eran demasiado tenues, a súa forma cambiaba con frecuencia nas cartas estelares. Dende a dinastía Song, fixouse como 2 UMi e HIP 112833. Máis tarde, debido ós cambios de posición dos *Asentos Interiores dos Cinco Emperadores*, durante as dinastías Yuan e Ming, o HIP 112833 foi substituído por HIP 113116."

#. Description of Korean constellation Great Emperor of Heaven
msgid ""
"*Great Emperor of Heaven* (Korean: 천황대제, Hanja: 天皇大帝, Romanization: Cheonhwangdaeje) is 1 star in the mouth of the *Curved Array*. In Taoism, the Heavenly Emperor is also known as the *Hook Array Emperor* because of its location in the *Curved Array*.\n"
"\n"
"He assists the Jade Emperor in governing the north and south celestial poles and the Three Powers (heaven, earth, and humanity), overseeing all stars, serving as the emperor of all celestial bodies and constellations, ruling over the stars, and managing all military and warfare affairs in the human world. Thus, he is regarded as the god of war and martial deity.\n"
"\n"
"Initially, the *Great Emperor of Heaven* corresponded to 2 UMi. However, with changes in the *Curved Array* constellation, the *Great Emperor of Heaven* was changed to HIP 115746 until the end of the Ming Dynasty. There are also a very few works that correspond the *Great Emperor of Heaven* to the brightest star α UMi of the *Curved Array*, but this is not mainstream."
msgstr ""
"*Gran Emperador do Ceo* (en coreano: 천황대제, en hanja: 天皇大帝, romanizado: Cheonhwangdaeje) é unha estrela situada na boca da *Matriz Curva*. No taoísmo, o Emperador Celestial tamén se coñece como *Emperador da Matriz de Ganchos* debido á súa localización na *Matriz Curva*.\n"
"\n"
"Axuda o Emperador de Xade a gobernar os polos celestes norte e sur e os Tres Poderes (ceo, terra e humanidade), supervisando todas as estrelas, servindo como emperador de todos os corpos celestes e constelacións, gobernando as estrelas e xestionando todos os asuntos militares e bélicos no mundo humano. Polo tanto, é considerado o deus da guerra e a divindade marcial.\n"
"\n"
"Inicialmente, o *Gran Emperador do Ceo* correspondía a 2 UMi. Non obstante, cos cambios na constelación da *Matriz Curva*, o *Gran Emperador do Ceo* cambiou a HIP 115746 ata o final da dinastía Ming. Tamén hai algúns traballos que fan corresponder o *Gran Emperador do Ceo* á estrela máis brillante α UMi da *Matriz Curva*, pero isto non é algo común."

#. Description of Korean constellation Six Jia
msgid ""
"*Six Jia* (Korean: 육갑, Hanja: 六甲, Romanization: Yukgap) consists of 6 stars "
"in the *Purple Forbidden Enclosure*, beside the *Canopy of the Emperor* and "
"*Canopy Support*. *Six Jia* refers to the six Heavenly Stems paired with "
"\"Jia\", including Jiazi, Jiaxu, Jiashen, Jiawu, Jiachen, and Jiayin. "
"Heavenly Stems and Earthly Branches are important timekeeping units in "
"China, also commonly used for counting, naming, and divination. This "
"constellation is used to determine the seasons in the celestial world, "
"manage yin and yang, and announce time to people, promulgating decrees and "
"promoting moral education."
msgstr ""
"*Six Jia* (coreano: 육갑, hanja: 六甲, romanizado: Yukgap) consta de 6 estrelas "
"no *Recinto Prohibido Púrpura*, onda o *Dosel do Emperador* e o *Soporte do "
"Dosel*. *Six Jia* refírese ós seis Talos Celestiais emparellados con "
"\"Jia\", incluíndo Jiazi, Jiaxu, Jiashen, Jiawu, Jiachen e Jiayin. Os Talos "
"Celestiais e as Ramas Terrestres son unidades importantes de medición do "
"tempo na China, tamén se usan habitualmente para contar, nomear e adiviñar. "
"Esta constelación utilízase para determinar as estacións no mundo celestial,"
" xestionar o yin e o yang e anunciar o tempo á xente, promulgar decretos e "
"promover a educación moral."

#. Description of Korean constellation Seats of the Five Emperors
msgid ""
"*Interior Seats of the Five Emperors* (Korean: 오제좌, Hanja: 五帝坐, "
"Romanization: Ojejwa) consists of 5 stars under the *Canopy of the Emperor*,"
" beside the *Canopy Support*. They are the seats of the Five Emperors of the"
" five directions. The Five Emperors include the Green Emperor, Red Emperor, "
"Yellow Emperor, White Emperor, and Black Emperor, corresponding to the east,"
" south, center, west, and north directions respectively."
msgstr ""
"Os *Asentos interiores dos Cinco Emperadores* (en coreano: 오제좌, en hanja: "
"五帝坐, romanizado: Ojejwa) constan de 5 estrelas baixo o *Dosel do Emperador*,"
" xunto ó *Soporte do Dosel*. Son os asentos dos Cinco Emperadores das cinco "
"direccións. Os Cinco Emperadores inclúen o Emperador Verde, o Emperador "
"Vermello, o Emperador Amarelo, o Emperador Branco e o Emperador Negro, "
"correspondentes ás direccións leste, sur, centro, oeste e norte, "
"respectivamente."

#. Description of Korean constellation Canopy of the Emperor
msgid ""
"*Canopy of the Emperor* (Korean: 화개, Hanja: 華蓋, Romanization: Hwagae) "
"consists of 7 stars above the *Great Emperor of Heaven*, at the back gate of"
" the *Purple Forbidden Enclosure*, just covering the *Great Emperor of "
"Heaven*. It is the umbrella used by the Emperor."
msgstr ""
"O *Dosel do Emperador* (en coreano: 화개, en hanja: 華蓋, romanizado: Hwagae) "
"consiste en 7 estrelas por riba do *Gran Emperador do Ceo*, na porta "
"traseira do *Recinto Púrpura Prohibido*, cubrindo xusto o *Gran Emperador do"
" Ceo*. É o paraugas que usa o Emperador."

#. Description of Korean constellation Canopy Support (Vassal of Canopy of the
#. Emperor)
msgid ""
"*Canopy Support* (Korean: 강, Hanja: 杠, Romanization: Gang) consists of 9 "
"stars under the *Canopy of the Emperor*, serving as the handle of the "
"canopy."
msgstr ""
"O *Soporte do Dosel* (coreano: 강, hanja: 杠, romanizado: Gang) consta de 9 "
"estrelas baixo o *Dosel do Emperador*, que serve como asa do dosel."

#. Description of Korean constellation Celestial Pillar
msgid ""
"*Celestial Pillar* (Korean: 천주, Hanja: 天柱, Romanization: Cheonju) consists "
"of 5 stars near the *Purple Forbidden East Wall*, close to the northern end "
"of the wall. They are pillars in the Heavenly Palace used for posting "
"decrees. Bans are often issued here at the beginning and middle of the month"
" to notify all officials."
msgstr ""
"O *Piar Celestial* (en coreano: 천주, en hanja: 天柱, romanizado: Cheonju) "
"consta de 5 estrelas preto do *Muro Leste Prohibido Púrpura*, preto do "
"extremo norte do muro. Son piares no Palacio Celestial que se usan para "
"publicar decretos. Habitualmente emítense prohibicións nel a principios e "
"mediados de mes para notificar a todos os funcionarios."

#. Description of Korean constellation Palace of the Maids-in-waiting
msgid ""
"*Maids-in-waiting* (Korean: 여어궁, Hanja: 女御宮, Romanization: Yeoeogung) "
"consists of 4 stars north of the *Curved Array*, serving as maids in the "
"palace."
msgstr ""
"As *Damas de compañía* (en coreano: 여어궁, en hanja: 女御宮, romanizado: "
"Yeoeogung) constan de 4 estrelas ó norte da *Matriz Curva*, que serven como "
"criadas no palacio."

#. Description of Korean constellation Official of Royal Archives
msgid ""
"*Official of Royal Archives* (Korean: 주하사, Hanja: 柱下史, Romanization: Juhasa)"
" is 1 star northeast of the *Northern Pole*, close to the *Royal Secretary*."
" It is a historian responsible for recording daily affairs in the palace."
msgstr ""
"*Funcionario dos Arquivos Reais* (en coreano: 주하사, en hanja: 柱下史, "
"romanizado: Juhasa) está situado a 1 estrela ó nordeste do *Polo Norte*, "
"preto do *Secretario Real*. É un historiador responsable de rexistrar os "
"asuntos diarios do palacio."

#. Description of Korean constellation Female Protocol
msgid ""
"*Female Protocol* (Korean: 여사, Hanja: 女史, Romanization: Yeosa) is 1 star "
"north of the *Official of Royal Archives*. It is a female official in charge"
" of timekeeping by water clock in the palace."
msgstr ""
"*Protocolo feminino* (coreano: 여사, hanja: 女史, romanizado: Yeosa) está "
"situado a 1 estrela ó norte do *Funcionario dos Arquivos Reais*. É unha "
"funcionaria encargada de controlar o tempo mediante un reloxo de auga no "
"palacio."

#. Description of Korean constellation Royal Secretary
msgid ""
"*Royal Secretary* (Korean: 상서, Hanja: 尚書, Romanization: Sangseo) consists of"
" 5 stars in the southeast corner of the *Purple Forbidden Enclosure*, inside"
" the south gate. It is an official responsible for documents and memorials, "
"offering advice to the Heavenly Emperor."
msgstr ""
"O *Secretario Real* (en coreano: 상서, en hanja: 尚書, romanizado Sangseo) "
"consta de 5 estrelas na esquina sueste do *Recinto Prohibido Púrpura*, "
"dentro da porta sur. É un funcionario responsable dos documentos e "
"memoriais, que ofrece consellos ó Emperador Celestial."

#. Description of Korean constellation Hidden Virtue
msgid ""
"*Hidden Virtue* (Korean: 음덕, Hanja: 陰德, Romanization: Eumdeok) consists of 2"
" stars inside the *Purple Forbidden Enclosure* gate, west of the *Royal "
"Secretary*. It refers to good deeds done in secret, in charge of benefiting "
"the people and providing relief and comfort."
msgstr ""
"*Virtude Oculta* (en coreano: 음덕, en hanja: 陰德, romanizado: Eumdeok) consta "
"de 2 estrelas dentro da porta do *Recinto Púrpura Prohibido*, ó oeste do "
"*Secretario Real*. Refírese ás boas accións realizadas en segredo, "
"encargadas de beneficiar a xente e proporcionar alivio e consolo."

#. Description of Korean constellation Chief Judge
msgid ""
"*Chief Judge* (Korean: 대리, Hanja: 大理, Romanization: Daeri) consists of 2 "
"stars inside the left star of the *Purple Forbidden Enclosure* gate, close "
"to *Hidden Virtue*. It is an official in charge of trial and punishment, "
"used for divining wrongful convictions."
msgstr ""
"*Xuíz xefe* (en coreano: 대리, en hanja: 大理, romanizado: Daeri) consta de 2 "
"estrelas dentro da estrela esquerda da porta *Recinto Púrpura Prohibido*, "
"preto da *Virtude Oculta*. É un funcionario encargado dos xuízos e castigos,"
" e adiviña condenas inxustas."

#. Description of Korean constellation Celestial Bed
msgid ""
"*Celestial Bed* (Korean: 천상, Hanja: 天床, Romanization: Cheonsang) consists of"
" 6 stars outside the *Purple Forbidden Enclosure* gate. It is the bed where "
"the Heavenly Emperor sleeps and rests."
msgstr ""
"*Cama Celestial* (en coreano: 천상, en hanja: 天床, romanizado: Cheonsang) "
"consta de 6 estrelas fóra da porta *Recinto Púrpura Prohibido*. É a cama "
"onde dorme e descansa o Emperador Celestial."

#. Description of Korean constellation Celestial One
msgid ""
"*Celestial Great One* (Korean: 천일, Hanja: 天一, Romanization: Cheon-il) is 1 "
"star outside the *Purple Forbidden Enclosure*, south of the right star of "
"the palace gate. It is the god of the Heavenly Emperor, governing the "
"operation of the Heavenly Tao, coordinating the twelve divine generals, and "
"presiding over wars and personal good fortune."
msgstr ""
"*O Grande Celestial* (en coreano: 천일, en hanja: 天一, romanizado: Cheon-il) é "
"unha estrela situada fóra do *Recinto Púrpura Prohibido*, ó sur da estrela "
"dereita da porta do palacio. É o deus do Emperador Celestial, que goberna o "
"funcionamento do Tao Celestial, coordina os doce xenerais divinos e preside "
"as guerras e a boa fortuna persoal."

#. Description of Korean constellation Supreme One
msgid ""
"*First Great One* (Korean: 태일, Hanja: 太一, Romanization: Taeil) is 1 star "
"south of *Celestial Great One*, close to it. It governs the sixteen gods and"
" is responsible for predicting natural disasters and social upheavals such "
"as wind, rain, floods, droughts, wars, famines, and plagues."
msgstr ""
"*O Grande Primeiro* (coreano: 태일, Hanja: 太一, romanizado: Taeil) é 1 estrela "
"ó sur de *O Grande Celestial*, preto dela. Goberna os dezaseis deuses e "
"encárgase de prever desastres naturais e trastornos sociais como vento, "
"choiva, inundacións, secas, guerras, fames e pestes."

#. Description of Korean constellation Inner Kitchen
msgid ""
"*Inner Kitchen* (Korean: 내주, Hanja: 內厨, Romanization: Naeju) consists of 2 "
"stars outside the southwest corner of the *Purple Forbidden Enclosure*, the "
"kitchen responsible for the palace's diet."
msgstr ""
"A *Cociña Interior* (en coreano: 내주, en hanja: 內厨, romanizado: Naeju) consta"
" de 2 estrelas fóra da esquina suroeste do *Recinto Púrpura Prohibido*, a "
"cociña responsable da dieta do palacio."

#. Description of Korean constellation Celestial Kitchen
msgid ""
"*Celestial Kitchen* (Korean: 천주, Hanja: 天厨, Romanization: Cheonju) consists "
"of 6 stars outside the northeast corner of the *Purple Forbidden Enclosure*,"
" the kitchen responsible for state banquet catering."
msgstr ""
"A *Cociña Celestial* (en coreano: 천주, en hanja: 天厨, romanizado: Cheonju) "
"consta de 6 estrelas fóra da esquina nordeste do *Recinto Púrpura "
"Prohibido*, a cociña responsable do cátering dos banquetes estatais."

#. Description of Korean constellation Guest House
msgid ""
"*Guest House* (Korean: 전사, Hanja: 傳舍, Romanization: Jeonsa) consists of 9 "
"stars outside the *Purple Forbidden Enclosure*, above the *Canopy of the "
"Emperor*, close to the Milky Way. It is a place for guests to stay."
msgstr ""
"*Casa de Hóspedes* (en coreano: 전사, en hanja: 傳舍, romanizado: Jeonsa) consta"
" de 9 estrelas fóra do *Recinto Púrpura Prohibido*, sobre o *Dosel do "
"Emperador*, preto da Vía Láctea. É un lugar onde se aloxan os hóspedes."

#. Description of Korean constellation Eight Kinds of Crops
msgid ""
"*Eight Kinds of Crops* (Korean: 팔곡, Hanja: 八穀, Romanization: Palgok) "
"consists of 8 stars north of the *Five Chariots*, in front of the *Inner "
"Steps*. The eight kinds of grain crops are rice, millet, barley, wheat, "
"soybeans, small beans, millet, and hemp. They are used for divining "
"agricultural harvests."
msgstr ""
"*Oito Tipos de Cultivos* (en coreano: 팔곡, en hanja: 八穀, romanizado: Palgok) "
"consta de 8 estrelas ó norte dos *Cinco Carros*, diante das *Escaleiras "
"Interiores*. Os oito tipos de cultivos de cereais son o arroz, o millo, a "
"cebada, o trigo, a soia, as fabas pequenas, o millo e o cáñamo. Úsanse para "
"adiviñar as colleitas agrícolas."

#. Description of Korean constellation Inner Steps
msgid ""
"*Inner Steps* (Korean: 내계, Hanja: 內階, Romanization: Naegye) consists of 6 "
"stars north of the *Administrative Center*, the steps for the Heavenly "
"Emperor to go up and down, connecting the back gate of the *Purple Forbidden"
" Enclosure* with the *Administrative Center*."
msgstr ""
"As *Escaleiras Interiores* (en coreano: 내계, en hanja: 內階, romanizado: "
"Naegye) constan de 6 estrelas ó norte do *Centro Administrativo*, as "
"escaleiras para que o Emperador Celestial suba e baixe, conectando a porta "
"traseira do *Recinto Púrpura Prohibido* co *Centro Administrativo*."

#. Description of Korean constellation Administrative Center
msgid ""
"*Administrative Center* (Korean: 문창, Hanja: 文昌, Romanization: Munchang) consists of 6 stars in front of the bowl of the *Northern Dipper* (the Big Dipper), west of the *Purple Forbidden Enclosure*, shaped like a half-moon and a basket, known as \"the dipper wearing a basket\". It is a collective name for six government departments or officials, including the *Great General*, *Second General*, *Distinguished Premier*, *Deified Judge of Life*, *Deified Judge of Central Affairs*, and *Deified Judge of Rank*, in charge of cultural education, etiquette and music, rewarding and punishing officials, adding salaries, and promoting officials to higher positions.\n"
"\n"
"There are two theories regarding the number of stars in this constellation: six or seven. The original version consisted of seven stars: ο, τ, 23, υ, φ, θ, 15 UMa. In later Chinese traditions, the six-star version became mainstream. During the Tang Dynasty, due to inaccuracies in star charting, the entire constellation rotated counterclockwise, leading to changes in the corresponding stars, which were then altered to 23, υ, φ, θ, 15, HIP 44504/18 UMa, making a total of six stars. However, the older version continued to circulate. The *Administrative Center* constellation depicted in the *Xianglin* star chart is the early, unaltered version."
msgstr ""
"*Centro Administrativo* (en coreano: 문창, en hanja: 文昌, romanizado: Munchang) consta de 6 estrelas diante da cunca da *Culler do Norte* (o Carro Maior), ó oeste do *Recinto Púrpura Prohibido*, con forma de media lúa e cesta, coñecido como \"o mergullador que leva unha cesta\". É un nome colectivo para seis departamentos ou funcionarios gobernamentais, incluíndo o *Gran Xeneral*, o *Segundo Xeneral*, o *Primeiro Ministro Distinguido*, o *Xuíz Deificado da Vida*, o *Xuíz Deificado de Asuntos Centrais* e o *Xuíz Deificado de Rango*, encargados da educación cultural, a etiqueta e a música, recompensando e castigando os funcionarios, engadindo salarios e ascendendo a funcionarios a postos máis altos.\n"
"\n"
"Hai dúas teorías sobre o número de estrelas nesta constelación: seis ou sete. A versión orixinal constaba de sete estrelas: ο, τ, 23, υ, φ, θ, 15 UMa. Nas tradicións chinesas posteriores, a versión de seis estrelas converteuse na corrente principal. Durante a dinastía Tang, debido a inexactitudes na representación das cartas estelares, toda a constelación xiraba en sentido antihorario, o que provocaba cambios nas estrelas correspondentes, que logo se alteraban a 23, υ, φ, θ, 15, HIP 44504/18 UMa, o que facía un total de seis estrelas. Non obstante, a versión máis antiga continuou a circular. A constelación do *Centro Administrativo* representada na carta estelar *Xianglin* é a versión primitiva e inalterada."

#. Description of Korean constellation Celestial Prison
msgid ""
"*Celestial Prison* (Korean: 천뢰, Hanja: 天牢, Romanization: Cheolloe) consists "
"of 6 stars under the bowl of *Northern Dipper*, a prison for detaining law-"
"breaking nobles."
msgstr ""
"A *Prisión Celestial* (en coreano: 천뢰, en hanja: 天牢, romanizado: Cheolloe) "
"consta de 6 estrelas baixo a cunca da *Cullere do Norte*, unha prisión para "
"deter nobres que infrinxen a lei."

#. Description of Korean constellation Three Excellencies (Wuxian)
msgid ""
"*Three Top Instructors* (Korean: 삼공, Hanja: 三公, Romanization: Samgong) "
"consists of 3 stars west of the first star (α UMa) of the bowl of the "
"*Northern Dipper*. The *Three Top Instructors* are the *Grand Protector*, "
"*Grand Tutor*, and *Grand Preceptor*, the highest officials responsible for "
"national military and political affairs."
msgstr ""
"Os *Tres Instrutores Superiores* (en coreano: 삼공, en hanja: 三公, romanizado: "
"Samgong) constan de 3 estrelas ó oeste da primeira estrela (α UMa) da conca "
"da *Culler do Norte*. Os *Tres Instrutores Superiores* son o *Gran "
"Protector*, o *Gran Titor* e o *Gran Preceptor*, os máis altos funcionarios "
"responsables dos asuntos militares e políticos nacionais."

#. Description of Korean constellation Northern Dipper
msgid ""
"*Northern Dipper* (Korean: 북두, Hanja: 北斗, Romanization: Bukdu) consists of 7 stars south of the *Purple Forbidden Enclosure*, corresponds to the Big Dipper in the West. The first 4 stars (α, β, γ, δ UMa) are called *Dou Kui* (the Bowl or Ladle's Head), and the last 3 stars (ε, ζ, η UMa) are called *Dou Bing* or *Dou Shao* (the Handle). Shaped like a ladle and located in the northern sky, it symbolizes the Heavenly Emperor's chariot.\n"
"\n"
"The *Northern Dipper* lies within the circumpolar circle, is highly distinctive, and its stars are bright. Therefore, it became a crucial constellation for determining direction and indicating the seasons. By using the *Northern Dipper*, one can easily locate other bright stars and constellations in the sky."
msgstr ""
"A *Culler do Norte* (en coreano: 북두, en hanja: 北斗, romanizado: Bukdu) consta de 7 estrelas ó sur do *Recinto Púrpura Prohibido* e corresponde á Osa Maior no oeste. As primeiras 4 estrelas (α, β, γ, δ UMa) chámanse *Dou Kui* (a cunca ou a cabeza da culler) e as últimas 3 estrelas (ε, ζ, η UMa) chámanse *Dou Bing* ou *Dou Shao* (o mango). Ten forma de culler, está situada no ceo setentrional e simboliza o carro do Emperador Celestial.\n"
"\n"
"A *Culler do Nortel* atópase dentro do círculo circumpolar, é moi distintiva e as súas estrelas son brillantes. Polo tanto, converteuse nunha constelación crucial para determinar a dirección e indicar as estacións. Usando o **Culler do Norte*, pódense localizar facilmente outras estrelas e constelacións brillantes no ceo."

#. Description of Korean constellation Assistant (Vassal of Northern Dipper)
msgid ""
"*Assistant* (Korean: 보, Hanja: 輔, Romanization: Bo) is 1 star, the prime "
"minister or minister assisting the *Northern Dipper*."
msgstr ""
"*Asistente* (coreano: 보, hanja: 輔, romanizado: Bo) é 1 estrela, o primeiro "
"ministro ou ministro que axuda a *Culler do Norte*."

#. Description of Korean constellation Judge for Nobility
msgid ""
"*Judge for Nobility* (Korean: 천리, Hanja: 天理, Romanization: Cheolli) consists"
" of 4 stars in the *Northern Dipper*'s dipper. It is a prison for nobles and"
" also a law enforcement official."
msgstr ""
"*Xuíz da Nobreza* (en coreano: 천리, en hanja: 天理, romanizado: Cheolli) consta"
" de 4 estrelas no cazo da *Culler do Nosrte*. É unha prisión para nobres e "
"tamén para axentes da lei."

#. Description of Korean constellation Three Excellencies (Gan School)
msgid ""
"*Three Excellencies* (Korean: 삼공, Hanja: 三公, Romanization: Samgong) consists"
" of 3 stars south of the *Northern Dipper*'s handle. The *Three "
"Excellencies* include the *Grand Commandant*, *Minister over the Masses*, "
"and *Minister of Works*, the same as the *Three Top Instructors*, three "
"highly respected official positions."
msgstr ""
"As *Tres Excelencias* (en coreano: 삼공, en hanja: 三公, romanizado: Samgong) "
"constan de 3 estrelas ó sur da asa da *Culler do Norte*. As *Tres "
"Excelencias* inclúen o *Gran Comandante*, o *Ministro das Masas* e o "
"*Ministro de Obras*, o mesmo que os *Tres Instrutores Superiores*, tres "
"cargos oficiais moi respectados."

#. Description of Korean constellation Prime Minister
msgid ""
"*Prime Minister* (Korean: 상, Hanja: 相, Romanization: Sang) is 1 star south "
"of the fourth star of the *Northern Dipper*. It is the prime minister, "
"assisting the Emperor in managing state affairs, the highest administrative "
"official under the monarch, leading all officials and holding military "
"power."
msgstr ""
"*Primeiro Ministro* (en coreano: 상, en hanja: 相, romanizado: Sang) é unha "
"estrela ó sur da cuarta estrela da *Culler do Norte*. É o primeiro ministro,"
" que axuda o emperador na xestión dos asuntos estatais, o funcionario "
"administrativo máis alto do monarca, dirixe todos os funcionarios e ostenta "
"o poder militar."

#. Description of Korean constellation Guard of the Sun
msgid ""
"*Guard of the Sun* (Korean: 태양수, Hanja: 太陽守, Romanization: Taeyangsu) is 1 "
"star southwest of the *Prime Minister*. It is a general responsible for "
"garrison and alert."
msgstr ""
"A *Garda do Sol* (en coreano: 태양수, en hanja: 太陽守, romanizado: Taeyangsu) "
"está situada a 1 estrela ó suroeste do *Primeiro Ministro*. É un xeneral "
"responsable da gornición e da alerta."

#. Description of Korean constellation Eunuch
msgid ""
"*Eunuch* (Korean: 세, Hanja: 勢, Romanization: Se) consists of 4 stars "
"northwest of the *Guard of the Sun*, officials who have been castrated, "
"specifically eunuchs."
msgstr ""
"*Eunuco* (coreano: 세, hanja: 勢, romanizado: Se) consta de 4 estrelas ó "
"noroeste da *Garda do Sol*, funcionarios que foron castrados, concretamente "
"eunucos."

#. Description of Korean constellation Sombre Lance
msgid ""
"*Sombre Lance* (Korean: 현과, Hanja: 玄戈, Romanization: Hyeongwa) is 1 star "
"north of the *Twinkling Indicator*, close to the *Celestial Spear* and one "
"end of the *Northern Dipper*. This is a weapon, a halberd, the celestial "
"lance or a weapon used by northern nomadic tribes. It is used to divine "
"whether northern nomadic tribes will invade."
msgstr ""
"A *Lanza Sombría* (coreano: 현과, Hanja: 玄戈, romanizado: Hyeongwa) é 1 estrela"
" ó norte do *Indicador Escintilante*, preto da *Lanza Celestial* e un "
"extremo da *Culler do Norte*. Trátase dunha arma, unha alabarda, a lanza "
"celeste ou unha arma utilizada polas tribos nómades do norte. Úsase para "
"adiviñar se as tribos nómades do norte invadirán."

#. Description of Korean constellation Celestial Spear
msgid ""
"*Celestial Spear* (Korean: 천창, Hanja: 天槍, Romanization: Cheonchang) consists"
" of 3 stars east of the *Northern Dipper*'s handle. It is a weapon for "
"defending the *Purple Forbidden Enclosure*."
msgstr ""
"*Lanza Celestial* (en coreano: 천창, en hanja: 天槍, romanizado: Cheonchang) "
"consta de 3 estrelas ó leste do mango da *Culler do Norte*. É unha arma para"
" defender o *Recinto Púrpura Prohibido*."

#. Description of Korean constellation Celestial Flail
msgid ""
"*Celestial Flail* (Korean: 천봉, Hanja: 天棓, Romanization: Cheonbong) consists "
"of 5 stars northeast of the *Woman's Bed*, a big stick, like the *Celestial "
"Spear*, also a defensive weapon."
msgstr ""
"O *Mallo Celestial* (coreano: 천봉, hanja: 天棓, romanizado: Cheonbong) consta "
"de 5 estrelas ó nordeste da *Cama da Muller*, un gran pau, como a *Lanza "
"Celestial*, tamén unha arma defensiva."

#. Description of Korean constellation Royals
msgid ""
"*Royals* (Korean: 태존, Hanja: 太尊, Romanization: Taejon) is 1 star north of "
"the *Middle Step*. It represents royal relatives."
msgstr ""
"A *Realeza* (coreano: 태존, Hanja: 太尊, romanizado: Taejon) é 1 estrela ó norte"
" do *Paso Medio*. Representa os parentes reais."

#. Description of Korean constellation Supreme Palace
msgid ""
"*Supreme Palace Enclosure* (Korean: 태미, Hanja: 太微, Romanization: Taemi) is "
"the Heavenly Court where the Heavenly Emperor handles government affairs, "
"mainly composed of various officials. The south gate is called the *Meridian"
" Gate*."
msgstr ""
"O *Recinto do Palacio Supremo* (en coreano: 태미, en hanja: 太微, romanizado: "
"Taemi) é a Corte Celestial onde o Emperador Celestial se encarga dos asuntos"
" gobernamentais, composta principalmente por varios funcionarios. A porta "
"sur chámase *Porta Meridiana*."

#. Description of Korean constellation Five Emperors
msgid ""
"*Seats of the Five Emperors* (Korean: 오제, Hanja: 五帝, Romanization: Oje) "
"consists of 5 stars in the center of the *Supreme Palace Enclosure*, the "
"seats of the Five Emperors of the five directions. In the *Purple Forbidden "
"Enclosure*, there is also the *Interior Seats of the Five Emperors*. The "
"central bright star (β Leo) is the seat of Yellow Emperor, symbolizing the "
"Son of Heaven."
msgstr ""
"*Os Asentos dos Cinco Emperadores* (en coreano: 오제, en hanja: 五帝, "
"romanizado: Oje) constan de 5 estrelas no centro do *Recinto do Palacio "
"Supremo*, os asentos dos Cinco Emperadores das cinco direccións. No *Recinto"
" Púrpura Prohibido*, tamén se atopan os *Asentos Interiores dos Cinco "
"Emperadores*. A estrela brillante central (β Leo) é o asento do Emperador "
"Amarelo, simbolizando o Fillo do Ceo."

#. Description of Korean constellation Inner Screen
msgid ""
"*Inner Screen* (Korean: 내병, Hanja: 內屏, Romanization: Naebyeong) consists of "
"4 stars inside the *Meridian Gate*, near the south of the *Seats of the Five"
" Emperors*, close to the *Right Law Administrator* (β Vir)."
msgstr ""
"A *Pantalla Interior* (en coreano: 내병, en hanja: 內屏, romanizado: Naebyeong) "
"consta de 4 estrelas dentro da *Porta Meridiana*, preto do sur dos *Asentos "
"dos Cinco Emperadores*, preto do *Administrador da Lei Dereito* (β Vir)."

#. Description of Korean constellation Usher to the Court
msgid ""
"*Usher to the Court* (Korean: 알자, Hanja: 謁者, Romanization: Alja) is 1 star "
"north of the *Left Law Administrator* (η Vir)."
msgstr ""
"*Uxier da Corte* (coreano: 알자, Hanja: 謁者, romanizado: Alja) é 1 estrela "
"ónorte do *Administrador da Lei da Esquerda* (η Vir)."

#. Description of Korean constellation Inner Seats of Three Excellencies
msgid ""
"*Three Excellencies* (Korean: 삼공내좌, Hanja: 三公內坐, Romanization: "
"Samgongnaejwa) consists of 3 stars, northeast of the *Usher to the Court*."
msgstr ""
"*Tres Excelencias* (coreano: 삼공내좌, Hanja: 三公內坐, romanizado: Samgongnaejwa) "
"consta de 3 estrelas, ó nordeste do *Uxier da Corte*."

#. Description of Korean constellation Nine Senior Officers
msgid ""
"*Nine Senior Officers* (Korean: 구경, Hanja: 九卿, Romanization: Gugyeong) "
"consists of 3 stars, north of the *Three Excellencies*."
msgstr ""
"Os *Nove Oficiais Superiores* (en coreano: 구경, en hanja: 九卿, romanizado: "
"Gugyeong) constan de 3 estrelas, ó norte das *Tres Excelencias*."

#. Description of Korean constellation Five Lords (In Supreme Palace
#. Enclosure)
msgid ""
"*Five Lords* (Korean: 오제후, Hanja: 五諸侯, Romanization: Ojehu) consists of 5 "
"stars, south of the *Officers of the Imperial Guard*."
msgstr ""
"Os *Cinco Señores* (en coreano: 오제후, en hanja: 五諸侯, romanizado: Ojehu) "
"constan de 5 estrelas situadas ó sur dos *Oficiais da Garda Imperial*."

#. Description of Korean constellation Crown Prince
msgid ""
"*Crown Prince* (Korean: 태자, Hanja: 太子, Romanization: Taeja) is 1 star north "
"of the *Seat of Yellow Emperor*."
msgstr ""
"O *Príncipe Herdeiro* (en coreano: 태자, en hanja: 太子, romanizado: Taeja) está"
" situado a 1 estrela ó norte do *Asento do Emperador Amarelo*."

#. Description of Korean constellation Retinue (In Supreme Palace Enclosure)
msgid ""
"*Retinue* (Korean: 종관, Hanja: 從官, Romanization: Jonggwan) is 1 star "
"northwest of the *Crown Prince*."
msgstr ""
"*O Séquito* (en coreano: 종관, en hanja: 從官, romanizado: Jonggwan) está "
"situada 1 estrela ó noroeste do *Príncipe Herdeiro*."

#. Description of Korean constellation Officer of Honour
msgid ""
"*Officer of Honour* (Korean: 행신, Hanja: 幸臣, Romanization: Haengsin) is 1 "
"star south of the *Crown Prince*, northeast of the *Seats of the Five "
"Emperors*."
msgstr ""
"*Oficial de Honra* (en coreano: 행신, en hanja: 幸臣, romanizado: Haengsin) está"
" situado a 1 estrela ó sur do *Príncipe Herdeiro* e ó nordeste dos *Asentos "
"dos Cinco Emperadores*."

#. Description of Korean constellation Officers of the Imperial Guard
msgid ""
"*Officers of the Imperial Guard* (Korean: 낭위, Hanja: 郎位, Romanization: "
"Nangwi) consists of 15 stars, northeast of the *Seats of the Five Emperors*."
msgstr ""
"Os *Oficiais da Garda Imperial* (en coreano: 낭위, en hanja: 郎位, romanizado: "
"Nangwi) constan de 15 estrelas situadas ó nordeste dos *Asentos dos Cinco "
"Emperadores*."

#. Description of Korean constellation Captain of the Bodyguards
msgid ""
"*Captain of the Bodyguards* (Korean: 낭장, Hanja: 郎將, Romanization: Nangjang) "
"is 1 star northeast of the *Officers of the Imperial Guard*."
msgstr ""
"O *Capitán dos Gardacostas*  (en coreano: 낭장, en hanja: 郎將, romanizado: "
"Nangjang) está situado a 1 estrela ó nordeste dos *Oficiais da Garda "
"Imperial*."

#. Description of Korean constellation Royal Guards
msgid ""
"*Royal Guards* (Korean: 상진, Hanja: 常陳, Romanization: Sangjin) consists of 7 "
"stars north of the *Seats of the Five Emperors*."
msgstr ""
"A *Garda Real* (en coreano: 상진, en hanja: 常陳, romanizado: Sangjin) consta de"
" 7 estrelas ó norte dos *Asentos dos Cinco Emperadores*."

#. Description of Korean constellation Emperor's Bodyguard
msgid ""
"*Emperor's Bodyguard* (Korean: 호분, Hanja: 虎賁, Romanization: Hobun) is 1 star"
" south of the *Lower Step*."
msgstr ""
"O *Gardacostas do Emperador* (en coreano: 호분, en hanja: 虎賁, romanizado: "
"Hobun) está a 1 estrela ó sur do *Chanzo Inferior*."

#. Description of Korean constellation Three Steps
msgid ""
"*Three Steps* (Korean: 삼대, Hanja: 三台, Romanization: Samdae) consists of 6 "
"stars, the *Three Steps* start from the *Administrative Center* and line up "
"in the *Supreme Palace Enclosure*."
msgstr ""
"Os *Tres Chanzos* (coreano: 삼대, hanja: 三台, romanizado: Samdae) constan de 6 "
"estrelas, os *Tres Chanzos* comezan no *Centro Administrativo* e aliñanse co"
" *Recinto do Palacio Supremo*."

#. Description of Korean constellation Three Steps (Upper Step)
msgid ""
"*Upper Step* (Korean: 삼대(상대)(三台(上台)), Romanization: Samdae(Sangdae)) as a "
"part of the *Three Steps*, consists of 2 stars."
msgstr ""
"*Chanzo Superior* (coreano: 삼대(상대)(三台(上台)), romanizado: Samdae(Sangdae)) "
"como parte dos *Tres Chanzos*, consta de 2 estrelas."

#. Description of Korean constellation Three Steps (Middle Step)
msgid ""
"*Middle Step* (Korean: 삼대(중대)(三台(中台)), Romanization: Samdae(Jungdae)) as a "
"part of the *Three Steps*, consists of 2 stars."
msgstr ""
"*Chanzo do medio* (coreano: 삼대(중대)(三台(中台)), romanizado: Samdae(Jungdae)) "
"como parte dos *Tres Chanzos*, consta de 2 estrelas."

#. Description of Korean constellation Three Steps (Lower Step)
msgid ""
"*Lower Step* (Korean: 삼대(하대)(三台(下台)), Romanization: Samdae(Hadae)) as a part"
" of the *Three Steps*, consists of 2 stars, north of the *Supreme Palace "
"West Wall*."
msgstr ""
"O *Chanzo Inferior* (en coreano: 삼대(하대)(三台(下台)), romanizado: Samdae(Hadae)),"
" como parte dos *Tres Chanzos*, consta de 2 estrelas, ó norte da *Muralla "
"Oeste do Palacio Supremo*."

#. Description of Korean constellation Junior Officers
msgid ""
"*Junior Officers* (Korean: 소미, Hanja: 少微, Romanization: Somi) consists of 4 "
"stars, lined up northwest of the *Supreme Palace Enclosure*."
msgstr ""
"*Oficiais Subalternos* (en coreano: 소미, en hanja: 少微, romanizado: Somi) "
"consta de 4 estrelas, aliñadas ó noroeste do *Recinto do Palacio Supremo*."

#. Description of Korean constellation Long Wall
msgid ""
"*Long Wall* (Korean: 장원, Hanja: 長垣, Romanization: Jangwon) consists of 4 "
"stars south of the *Junior Officers*."
msgstr ""
"*Muralla Longa* (en coreano: 장원, en hanja: 長垣, romanizado: Jangwon) consta "
"de 4 estrelas ó sur dos *Oficiais Subalternos*."

#. Description of Korean constellation Astronomical Observatory
msgid ""
"*Astronomical Observatory* (Korean: 영대, Hanja: 靈臺, Romanization: Yeongdae) "
"consists of 3 stars west of the *Hall of Glory*."
msgstr ""
"O *Observatorio Astronómico* (en coreano: 영대, en hanja: 靈臺, romanizado: "
"Yeongdae) consta de 3 estrelas ó oeste do *Salón da Gloria*."

#. Description of Korean constellation The Hall of Glory
msgid ""
"*The Hall of Glory* (Korean: 명당, Hanja: 明堂, Romanization: Myeongdang) "
"consists of 3 stars outside the southwest corner of the *Supreme Palace "
"Enclosure*."
msgstr ""
"O *Salón da Gloria* (en coreano: 명당, en hanja: 明堂, romanizado: Myeongdang) "
"consta de 3 estrelas fóra da esquina suroeste do *Recinto do Palacio "
"Supremo*."

#. Description of Korean constellation Heavenly Market
msgid ""
"*Heavenly Market Enclosure* (Korean: 천시, Hanja: 天市, Romanization: Cheonsi) "
"is the market in the sky."
msgstr ""
"O *Recinto do Mercado Celestial* (en coreano: 천시, en hanja: 天市, romanizado: "
"Cheonsi) é o mercado no ceo."

#. Description of Korean constellation Emperor's Seat
msgid ""
"*Emperor's Seat* (Korean: 제좌, Hanja: 帝座, Romanization: Jejwa) is 1 star in "
"the *Heavenly Market Enclosure*, west of the *Astrologer*."
msgstr ""
"O *Asento do Emperador* (en coreano: 제좌, en hanja: 帝座, romanizado: Jejwa) é "
"unha estrela no *Recinto do Mercado Celestial*, ó oeste do *Astrólogo*."

#. Description of Korean constellation Astrologer
msgid ""
"*Astrologer* (Korean: 후, Hanja: 候, Romanization: Hu) is 1 star northeast of "
"the *Emperor's Seat*."
msgstr ""
"*Astrólogo* (coreano: 후, Hanja: 候, romanizado: Hu) é 1 estrela ó nordeste do"
" *Asento do Emperador*."

#. Description of Korean constellation Eunuch Official
msgid ""
"*Eunuch Official* (Korean: 환자, Hanja: 宦者, Romanization: Hwanja) consists of "
"4 stars west of the *Emperor's Seat*."
msgstr ""
"O *Eunuco Oficial* (en coreano: 환자, en hanja: 宦者, romanizado: Hwanja) consta"
" de 4 estrelas ó oeste do *Asento do Emperador*."

#. Description of Korean constellation Official for the Royal Clan
msgid ""
"*Official for the Royal Clan* (Korean: 종정, Hanja: 宗正, Romanization: "
"Jongjeong) consists of 2 stars southeast of the *Emperor's Seat*."
msgstr ""
"*Oficial para o Clan Real* (coreano: 종정, hanja: 宗正, romanizado: Jongjeong) "
"consta de 2 estrelas ó sueste do *Asento do Emperador*."

#. Description of Korean constellation Official of Religious Ceremonies
msgid ""
"*Official of Religious Ceremonies* (Korean: 종인, Hanja: 宗人, Romanization: "
"Jongin) consists of 4 stars east of the *Official for the Royal Clan*."
msgstr ""
"*Oficial de Cerimonias Relixiosas* (coreano: 종인, hanja: 宗人, romanizado: "
"Jongin) consta de 4 estrelas ó leste do *Oficial do Clan Real*."

#. Description of Korean constellation Patriarchal Clan Stars
msgid ""
"*Patriarchal Clan Stars* (Korean: 종성, Hanja: 宗星, Romanization: Jongseong) "
"consists of 2 stars north of the *Official of Religious Ceremonies*, east of"
" the *Astrologer*."
msgstr ""
"As *Estrelas do Clan Patriarcal* (en coreano: 종성, en hanja: 宗星, romanizado: "
"Jongseong) constan de 2 estrelas ío norte do *Oficial de Cerimonias "
"Relixiosas* e ó leste do *Astrólogo*."

#. Description of Korean constellation Municipal Office
msgid ""
"*Municipal Office* (Korean: 시루, Hanja: 市樓, Romanization: Siru) consists of 6"
" stars in the market, above the *Winnowing Basket*."
msgstr ""
"*Oficina Municipal* (en coreano: 시루, en hanja: 市樓, romanizado: Siru) consta "
"de 6 estrelas no mercado, por riba da *Peneira*."

#. Description of Korean constellation Commodity Market
msgid ""
"*Commodity Market* (Korean: 거사, Hanja: 車肆, Romanization: Geosa) consists of "
"2 stars inside the right star of the *Heavenly Market Enclosure* gate."
msgstr ""
"O *Mercado de Produtos Básicos* (en coreano: 거사, en hanja: 車肆, romanizado: "
"Geosa) consta de 2 estrelas dentro da estrela dereita da porta do *Recinto "
"do Mercado Celestial*."

#. Description of Korean constellation Dipper for Solids
msgid ""
"*Dipper for Solids* (Korean: 곡, Hanja: 斛, Romanization: Gok) consists of 4 "
"stars in the market, south of the *Dipper for Liquids*."
msgstr ""
"*Culler lpara Sólidos* (coreano: 곡, Hanja: 斛, romanizado: Gok) consta de 4 "
"estrelas no mercado, ó sur do *Culler para Líquidos*."

#. Description of Korean constellation Dipper for Liquids
msgid ""
"*Dipper for Liquids* (Korean: 두, Hanja: 斗, Romanization: Du) consists of 5 "
"stars southwest of the *Eunuch Official*."
msgstr ""
"A *Culler para Líquidos* (coreano: 두, hanja: 斗, romanizado: Du) consta de 5 "
"estrelas ó suroeste do *Eunuco Oficial*."

#. Description of Korean constellation Jewel Market
msgid ""
"*Jewel Market* (Korean: 열사, Hanja: 列肆, Romanization: Yeolsa) consists of 2 "
"stars in the *Heavenly Market Enclosure*, northwest of the *Dipper for "
"Solids*."
msgstr ""
"O *Mercado de Xoias* (en coreano: 열사, en hanja: 列肆, romanizado: Yeolsa) "
"consta de 2 estrelas no *Recinto do Mercado Celestial*, ói noroeste de "
"*Culler de Sólidos*."

#. Description of Korean constellation Textile Ruler
msgid ""
"*Textile Ruler* (Korean: 백도, Hanja: 帛度, Romanization: Baekdo) consists of 2 "
"stars northeast of the *Patriarchal Clan Stars*."
msgstr ""
"*Regra Téxtil* (coreano: 백도, hanja: 帛度, romanizado: Baekdo) consta de 2 "
"estrelas ó nordeste das *Estrelas do Clan Patriarcal*."

#. Description of Korean constellation Butcher's Shops
msgid ""
"*Butcher's Shops* (Korean: 도사, Hanja: 屠肆, Romanization: Dosa) consists of 2 "
"stars north of the *Textile Ruler*."
msgstr ""
"*Carnicerías* (en coreano: 도사, en hanja: 屠肆, romanizado: Dosa) consta de 2 "
"estrelas ónorte da *Regra Téxtil*."

#. Description of Korean constellation Celestial Discipline
msgid ""
"*Celestial Discipline* (Korean: 천기, Hanja: 天紀, Romanization: Cheongi) "
"consists of 9 stars east of the *Coiled Thong*."
msgstr ""
"A *Disciplina Celestial* (en coreano: 천기, en hanja: 天紀, romanizado: Cheongi)"
" consta de 9 estrelas ó leste da *Correa Enrolada*."

#. Description of Korean constellation Woman's Bed
msgid ""
"*Woman's Bed* (Korean: 여상, Hanja: 女牀, Romanization: Yeosang) consists of 3 "
"stars north of the *Celestial Discipline*."
msgstr ""
"*Cama de muller* (en coreano: 여상, en hanja: 女牀, romanizado: Yeosang) consta "
"de 3 estrelas ó norte da *Disciplina Celestial*."

#. Description of Korean constellation Coiled Thong
msgid ""
"*Coiled Thong* (Korean: 관색, Hanja: 貫索, Romanization: Gwansaek) consists of 9"
" stars in front of the *Seven Excellencies*."
msgstr ""
"*Correa Enrolada* (en coreano: 관색, en hanja: 貫索, romanizado: Gwansaek) "
"consta de 9 estrelas diante das *Sete Excelencias*."

#. Description of Korean constellation Seven Excellencies
msgid ""
"*Seven Excellencies* (Korean: 칠공, Hanja: 七公, Romanization: Chilgong) "
"consists of 7 stars east of the *Twinkling Indicator*."
msgstr ""
"*Sete Excelencias* (coreano: 칠공, Hanja: 七公, romanizado: Chilgong) consta de "
"7 estrelas ó leste do *Indicador Escintilante*."

#. Description of Korean constellation Horn
msgid "*Horn* (Korean: 각, Hanja: 角, Romanization: Gak) consists of 2 stars."
msgstr ""
"*Corno* (en coreano: 각, en hanja: 角, romanizado: Gak) consta de 2 estrelas."

#. Description of Korean constellation Flat Road
msgid ""
"*Flat Road* (Korean: 평도, Hanja: 平道, Romanization: Pyeongdo) consists of 2 "
"stars beside the *Left Horn* (α Vir) and the *Right Horn* (ζ Vir)."
msgstr ""
"*Estrada Plana* (en coreano: 평도, en hanja: 平道, romanizado: Pyeongdo) consta "
"de 2 estrelas xunto á *Corna Esquerda* (α Vir) e á *Corna Dereita* (ζ Vir)."

#. Description of Korean constellation Recommending Virtuous Men
msgid ""
"*Recommending Virtuous Men* (Korean: 진현, Hanja: 進賢, Romanization: Jinhyeon) "
"is 1 star west of the *Flat Road*."
msgstr ""
"*Recomendando Homes Virtuosos* (en coreano: 진현, en hanja: 進賢, romanizado: "
"Jinhyeon) está a 1 estrela ó oeste da *Estrada Plana*."

#. Description of Korean constellation Celestial Farmland (In Horn Mansion)
msgid ""
"*Celestial Farmland* (Korean: 천전, Hanja: 天田, Romanization: Cheonjeon) "
"consists of 2 stars north of the *Right Horn* (ζ Vir)."
msgstr ""
"*Terras de Cultivo Celestiais* (en coreano: 천전, en hanja: 天田, romanizado: "
"Cheonjeon) consta de 2 estrelas ó norte do *Corna dereita* (ζ Vir)."

#. Description of Korean constellation Tripod of the Zhou
msgid ""
"*Tripod of the Zhou* (Korean: 주정, Hanja: 周鼎, Romanization: Jujeong) consists"
" of 3 stars west of the *Right Conductor*, above the *Horn Mansion*."
msgstr ""
"*Trípode dos Zhou* (coreano: 주정, Hanja: 周鼎, romanizado: Jujeong) consta de 3"
" estrelas ó oeste do *Conductor Dereito*, por riba da *Mansión dos Cornos*."

#. Description of Korean constellation Celestial Gate
msgid ""
"*Celestial Gate* (Korean: 천문, Hanja: 天門, Romanization: Cheonmun) consists of"
" 2 stars south of the *Left Horn* (α Vir), north of the *Judging Stars*."
msgstr ""
"A *Porta Celestial* (en coreano: 천문, en hanja: 天門, romanizado: Cheonmun) "
"consta de 2 estrelas ó sur do *Corna Esquerda* (α Vir), ó norte das "
"*Estrelas do Xuízo*."

#. Description of Korean constellation Judging
msgid ""
"*Judging Stars* (Korean: 평, Hanja: 平, Romanization: Pyeong) consists of 2 "
"stars north of the *Arsenal*."
msgstr ""
"*Estrelas do xuízo* (en coreano: 평, en hanja: 平, romanizado: Pyeong) constan"
" de 2 estrelas ó norte do *Arsenal*."

#. Description of Korean constellation Arsenal
msgid ""
"*Arsenal* (Korean: 고루, Hanja: 庫樓, Romanization: Goru) consists of 10 stars "
"south of the *Horn Mansion*."
msgstr ""
"*Arsenal* (en coreano: 고루, en hanja: 庫樓, romanizado: Goru) consta de 10 "
"estrelas ó sur da *Mansión dos Cornos*."

#. Description of Korean constellation Pillars (In Horn Mansion)
msgid ""
"*Pillars* (Korean: 주, Hanja: 柱, Romanization: Ju) consists of 15 stars."
msgstr ""
"*Piares* (en coreano: 주, en hanja: 柱, romanizado: Ju) constan de 15 "
"estrelas."

#. Description of Korean constellation Railings
msgid ""
"*Railings* (Korean: 형, Hanja: 衡, Romanization: Hyeong) consists of 4 stars."
msgstr ""
"*Varandas* (en coreano: 형, en hanja: 衡, romanizado: Hyeong) consta de 4 "
"estrelas."

#. Description of Korean constellation Southern Gate
msgid ""
"*Southern Gate* (Korean: 남문, Hanja: 南門, Romanization: Nammun) consists of 2 "
"stars south of the *Arsenal*."
msgstr ""
"A *Porta do Sur* (en coreano: 남문, en hanja: 南門, romanizado: Nammun) consta "
"de 2 estrelas ó sur do *Arsenal*."

#. Description of Korean constellation Neck
msgid "*Neck* (Korean: 항, Hanja: 亢, Romanization: Hang) consists of 4 stars."
msgstr ""
"*Pescozo* (en coreano: 항, en hanja: 亢, romanizado: Hang) ten 4 estrelas."

#. Description of Korean constellation Great Horn
msgid ""
"*Great Horn* (Korean: 대각, Hanja: 大角, Romanization: Daegak) is 1 star between"
" the left and right *Conductors*."
msgstr ""
"O *Gran Corno* (en coreano: 대각, en hanja: 大角, romanizado: Daegak) está "
"situado a 1 estrela entre os *Condutores* esquerdo e dereito."

#. Description of Korean constellation Conductor
msgid ""
"*Left Conductor* (Korean: 섭제, Hanja: 攝提, Romanization: Saptje) consists of 3 stars. The left and right *Conductors* sandwiching the *Great Horn*\n"
"\n"
"*Right Conductor* (Korean: 섭제, Hanja: 攝提, Romanization: Saptje) consists of 3 stars, directly south of the handle of the *Northern Dipper*. The left and right *Conductors* sandwiching the *Great Horn*"
msgstr ""
"O *Condutor Esquerdo* (en coreano: 섭제, en hanja: 攝提, romanización: Saptje) consta de 3 estrelas. Os *Condutores* esquerdo e dereito rodean o *Gran Corno*\n"
"\n"
"O *Condutor Dereito* (en coreano: 섭제, en hanja: 攝提, romanizado: Saptje) consta de 3 estrelas, directamente ó sur do mango da *Culler do Norte*. Os *Condutores* esquerdo e dereito rodean o *Gran Corno*"

#. Description of Korean constellation Executions
msgid ""
"*Executions* (Korean: 절위, Hanja: 折威, Romanization: Jeolwi) consists of 7 "
"stars south of the *Neck Mansion*."
msgstr ""
"*Execucións* (en coreano: 절위, en hanja: 折威, romanizado: Jeolwi) consta de 7 "
"estrelas ó sur da *Mansión do Pescozo*."

#. Description of Korean constellation Trials
msgid ""
"*Trials* (Korean: 돈완, Hanja: 頓頑, Romanization: Donwan) consists of 2 stars "
"southeast of the *Executions*."
msgstr ""
"*Probas* (coreano: 돈완, hanja: 頓頑, romaniizado: Donwan) consta de 2 estrelas "
"ó sueste das *Execucións*."

#. Description of Korean constellation Gate of Yang
msgid ""
"*Gate of Yang* (Korean: 양문, Hanja: 陽門, Romanization: Yangmun) consists of 2 "
"stars north of the *Arsenal*."
msgstr ""
"A *Porta do Yang* (en coreano: 양문, en hanja: 陽門, romanizado: Yangmun) consta"
" de 2 estrelas ó norte do *Arsenal*."

#. Description of Korean constellation Root
msgid "*Root* (Korean: 저, Hanja: 氐, Romanization: Jeo) consists of 4 stars."
msgstr "*Raíz* (coreano: 저, hanja: 氐, romanizado: Jeo) consta de 4 estrelas."

#. Description of Korean constellation Celestial Lance
msgid ""
"*Celestial Lance* (Korean: 경하, Hanja: 梗河, Romanization: Gyeongha) consists "
"of 3 stars north of the *Great Horn*, north of the *Mattress of the "
"Emperor*."
msgstr ""
"*Lanza Celestial* (coreano: 경하, hanja: 梗河, romanizado: Gyeongha) consta de 3"
" estrelas ó norte do *Gran Corno*, ó norte do *Colchón do Emperador*."

#. Description of Korean constellation Twinkling Indicator
msgid ""
"*Twinkling Indicator* (Korean: 초요, Hanja: 招搖, Romanization: Choyo) is 1 star"
" north of the *Celestial Lance*."
msgstr ""
"O *Indicador Escintilante* (en coreano: 초요, en hanja: 招搖, romanizado: Choyo)"
" está situado a 1 estrela ó norte da *Lanza Celestial*."

#. Description of Korean constellation Mattress of the Emperor
msgid ""
"*Mattress of the Emperor* (Korean: 제석, Hanja: 帝席, Romanization: Jeseok) "
"consists of 3 stars east of the *Great Horn*."
msgstr ""
"O *Colchón do Emperador* (en coreano: 제석, en hanja: 帝席, romanizado: Jeseok) "
"consta de 3 estrelas ó leste do *Gran Corno*."

#. Description of Korean constellation Boats and Lake
msgid ""
"*Boats and Lake* (Korean: 항지, Hanja: 亢池, Romanization: Hangji) consists of 6"
" stars north of the *Neck Mansion*."
msgstr ""
"*Barcos e Lago* (en coreano: 항지, en hanja: 亢池, romanizado: Hangji) consta de"
" 6 estrelas ó norte da *Mansión do Pescozo*."

#. Description of Korean constellation Celestial Milk
msgid ""
"*Celestial Milk* (Korean: 천유, Hanja: 天乳, Romanization: Cheonyu) is 1 star "
"northeast of the *Root Mansion*."
msgstr ""
"*Leite Celestial* (coreano: 천유, Hanja: 天乳, romanizado: Cheonyu) é 1 estrela "
"ó nordeste da *Mansión da Raíz*."

#. Description of Korean constellation Battle Chariots
msgid ""
"*Battle Chariots* (Korean: 진거, Hanja: 陣車, Romanization: Jingeo) consists of "
"3 stars south of the *Root Mansion*."
msgstr ""
"*Carros de Batalla* (en coreano: 진거, en hanja: 陣車, romanizado: Jingeo) "
"consta de 3 estrelas ó sur da *Mansión da Raíz*."

#. Description of Korean constellation Celestial Spokes
msgid ""
"*Celestial Spokes* (Korean: 천복, Hanja: 天輻, Romanization: Cheonbok) consists "
"of 2 stars, diagonally lined west of the *Room Mansion*."
msgstr ""
"*Raios Celestes* (en coreano: 천복, en hanja: 天輻, romanizado: Cheonbok) consta"
" de 2 estrelas, aliñadas diagonalmente ó oeste da *Mansión da Habitación*."

#. Description of Korean constellation Imperial Guards
msgid ""
"*Imperial Guards* (Korean: 기관, Hanja: 騎官, Romanization: Gigwan) consists of "
"27 stars south of the *Root Mansion*."
msgstr ""
"A *Garda Imperial* (en coreano: 기관, en hanja: 騎官, romanizado: Gigwan) consta"
" de 27 estrelas ó sur da *Mansión da Raíz*."

#. Description of Korean constellation Chariots and Cavalry
msgid ""
"*Chariots and Cavalry* (Korean: 거기, Hanja: 車騎, Romanization: Geogi) consists"
" of 3 stars south of the *Imperial Guards*."
msgstr ""
"*Carros e Cabalería* (en coreano: 거기, en hanja: 車騎, romanizado: Geogi) "
"consta de 3 estrelas ó sur da *Garda Imperial*."

#. Description of Korean constellation Chariots and Cavalry General
msgid ""
"*Chariots and Cavalry General* (Korean: 기진장군, Hanja: 騎陣將軍, Romanization: "
"Gijinjanggun) is 1 star at the eastern end of the *Imperial Guards*."
msgstr ""
"*Xeneral de Carros e Cabalería* (coreano: 기진장군, Hanja: 騎陣將軍, "
"romanizado:iGijinjanggun) é 1 estrela no extremo oriental das *Gardas "
"Imperiais*."

#. Description of Korean constellation Room
msgid "*Room* (Korean: 방, Hanja: 房, Romanization: Bang) consists of 4 stars."
msgstr ""
"*Habitación* (en coreano: 방, en hanja: 房, romanizado: Bang) ten 4 estrelas."

#. Description of Korean constellation Lock (Vassal of Room)
msgid ""
"*Lock* (Korean: 구검, Hanja: 鈎鈐, Romanization: Gugeom) consists of 2 stars "
"north of the *Room Mansion*."
msgstr ""
"*Peche* (en coreano: 구검, en hanja: 鈎鈐, romanizado: Gugeom) consta de 2 "
"estrelas ó norte da *Mansion da Habitación*."

#. Description of Korean constellation Door Bolt
msgid ""
"*Door Bolt* (Korean: 건폐, Hanja: 鍵閉, Romanization: Geonpye) is 1 star "
"northeast of the *Room Mansion*."
msgstr ""
"*Manilla da Porta* (coreano: 건폐, Hanja: 鍵閉, romanizado: Geonpye) é 1 estrela"
" ó nordeste da *Mansión da Habitación*."

#. Description of Korean constellation Punishment
msgid ""
"*Punishment* (Korean: 벌, Hanja: 罰, Romanization: Beol) consists of 3 stars "
"west of the *Eastern Door*, lined north-south."
msgstr ""
"*Castigo* (coreano: 벌, hanja: 罰, romanizado: Beol) consta de 3 estrelas ó "
"oeste da *Porta Oriental*, aliñadas de norte a sur."

#. Description of Korean constellation Eastern Door
msgid ""
"*Eastern Door* (Korean: 동함, Hanja: 東咸, Romanization: Dongham) consists of 4 "
"stars northeast of the *Room Mansion*."
msgstr ""
"A *Porta Leste* (en coreano: 동함, en hanja: 東咸, romanizado: Dongham) consta "
"de 4 estrelas ó nordeste da *Mansión da Habitación*."

#. Description of Korean constellation Western Door
msgid ""
"*Western Door* (Korean: 서함, Hanja: 西咸, Romanization: Seoham) consists of 4 "
"stars north of the *Room Mansion*."
msgstr ""
"A *Porta Oeste* (coreano: 서함, Hanja: 西咸, romanizado: Seoham) consta de 4 "
"estrelas ónorte da *Mansión da Habitación*."

#. Description of Korean constellation Solar Star
msgid ""
"*Solar Star* (Korean: 일, Hanja: 日, Romanization: Il) is 1 star in the middle"
" path of the *Room Mansion*."
msgstr ""
"*Estrela Solar* (en coreano: 일, en hanja: 日, romanizado: Il) é unha estrela "
"situada no camiño central da *Mansión da Habitación*."

#. Description of Korean constellation Retinue (In Room Mansion)
msgid ""
"*Retinue* (Korean: 종관, Hanja: 從官, Romanization: Jonggwan) consists of 2 "
"stars south of the *Room Mansion* stars."
msgstr ""
"*Séquito* (en coreano: 종관, en hanja: 從官, romanizado: Jonggwan) consta de 2 "
"estrelas ó sur das estrelas *Mansión da Habitación*."

#. Description of Korean constellation Heart
msgid "*Heart* (Korean: 심, Hanja: 心, Romanization: Sim) consists of 3 stars."
msgstr ""
"*Corazón* (en coreano: 심, en hanja: 心, romanizado: Sim) consta de 3 "
"estrelas."

#. Description of Korean constellation Group of Soldiers
msgid ""
"*Group of Soldiers* (Korean: 적졸, Hanja: 積卒, Romanization: Jeokjol) consists "
"of 12 stars south of the *Room Mansion*."
msgstr ""
"O *Grupo de Soldados* (en coreano: 적졸, en hanja: 積卒, romanizado: Jeokjol) "
"consta de 12 estrelas ósur da *Mansión daHabitación*."

#. Description of Korean constellation Tail
msgid "*Tail* (Korean: 미, Hanja: 尾, Romanization: Mi) consists of 9 stars."
msgstr "*Rabo* (coreano: 미, hanja: 尾, romanizado: Mi) consta de 9 estrelas."

#. Description of Korean constellation Changing Room (Vassal of Tail)
msgid ""
"*Changing Room* (Korean: 신궁, Hanja: 神宮, Romanization: Singung) is 1 star "
"beside the second star of the *Tail Mansion* (μ1 Sco)."
msgstr ""
"*Vestiario* (coreano: 신궁, Hanja: 神宮, romanizado: Singung) é 1 estrela onda a"
" segunda estrela da *Mansión do Rabo* (μ1 Sco)."

#. Description of Korean constellation Celestial River
msgid ""
"*Celestial River* (Korean: 천강, Hanja: 天江, Romanization: Cheongang) consists "
"of 4 stars north of the *Tail Mansion*."
msgstr ""
"*Río Celestial* (en coreano: 천강, en hanja: 天江, romanizado: Cheongang) consta"
" de 4 estrelas ó norte da *Mansión do Rabo*."

#. Description of Korean constellation Fu Yue
msgid ""
"*Fu Yue* (Korean: 부열, Hanja: 傅說, Romanization: Buyeol) is 1 star behind the "
"*Tail Mansion*."
msgstr ""
"*Fu Yue* (coreano: 부열, Hanja: 傅說, romanizado: Buyeol) está 1 estrela detrás "
"da *Mansión do Rabo*."

#. Description of Korean constellation Fish
msgid ""
"*Fish* (Korean: 어, Hanja: 魚, Romanization: Eo) is 1 star in the milky way "
"behind the *Tail Mansion*."
msgstr ""
"*Peixe* (coreano: 어, hanja: 魚, romanizado: Eo) está situado a 1 estrela na "
"Vía Láctea, detrás da *Mansión do Rabo"

#. Description of Korean constellation Tortoise
msgid ""
"*Tortoise* (Korean: 귀, Hanja: 龜, Romanization: Gwi) consists of 5 stars "
"south of the *Tail Mansion*."
msgstr ""
"*Tartaruga* (coreano: 귀, hanja: 龜, romanizado: Gwi) consta de 5 estrelas ó "
"sur da *Mansión do Rabo*."

#. Description of Korean constellation Winnowing Basket
msgid ""
"*Winnowing Basket* (Korean: 기, Hanja: 箕, Romanization: Gi) consists of 4 "
"stars."
msgstr ""
"*Peneira* (en coreano: 기, en hanja: 箕, romanizado: Gi) consta de 4 estrelas."

#. Description of Korean constellation Chaff
msgid ""
"*Chaff* (Korean: 강, Hanja: 糠, Romanization: Gang) is 1 star in front of the "
"*Winnowing Basket Mansion*'s tongue, northwest of the *Pestle*."
msgstr ""
"*Palla* (coreano: 강, hanja: 糠, romanizado: Gang) está situada 1 estrela "
"diante da lingua da *Mansión da Peneira*, ó noroeste da *Maza*."

#. Description of Korean constellation Outer Pestle
msgid ""
"*Pestle* (Korean: 외저, Hanja: 外杵, Romanization: Oejeo) consists of 3 stars "
"south of the *Winnowing Basket Mansion*."
msgstr ""
"*Pailán* (en coreano: 외저, en hanja: 外杵, romanizado: Oejeo) consta de 3 "
"estrelas ó sur da *Mansión da Peneira*."

#. Description of Korean constellation South Dipper
msgid ""
"*Dipper* (Korean: 남두, Hanja: 南斗, Romanization: Namdu) or *Southern Dipper*, "
"consists of 6 stars."
msgstr ""
"*Culler* (coreano: 남두, hanja: 南斗, romanizado: Namdu) ou *Culler do Sur*, "
"consta de 6 estrelas."

#. Description of Korean constellation Establishment Stars
msgid ""
"*Establishment Stars* (Korean: 건성, Hanja: 建星, Romanization: Geonseong) "
"consists of 6 stars north of the *Southern Dipper*."
msgstr ""
"As *Estrelas do Establecemento* (en coreano: 건성, en hanja: 建星, romanizado: "
"Geonseong) constan de 6 estrelas ó norte da *Culler do Sur*."

#. Description of Korean constellation Market Officer
msgid ""
"*Market Officer* (Korean: 천변, Hanja: 天弁, Romanization: Cheonbyeon) consists "
"of 9 stars north of the *Establishment Stars*."
msgstr ""
"*Oficial de mercado* (coreano: 천변, hanja: 天弁, romanización: Cheonbyeon) "
"consta de 9 estrelas ó norte das *Estrelas do establecemento*."

#. Description of Korean constellation Celestial Keyhole
msgid ""
"*Celestial Keyhole* (Korean: 천약, Hanja: 天鑰, Romanization: Cheonyak) consists"
" of 8 stars west of the second star of the *Southern Dipper*'s handle."
msgstr ""
"*O Burato da Fechadura Celestial* (en coreano: 천약, en hanja: 天鑰, romanizado:"
" Cheonyak) consta de 8 estrelas ó oeste da segunda estrela do mango da "
"*Culler do Sur*."

#. Description of Korean constellation Peasant
msgid ""
"*Peasant* (Korean: 농장인, Hanja: 農丈人, Romanization: Nongjangin) is 1 star "
"southwest of the *Southern Dipper*."
msgstr ""
"* Labrego* ( coreano : 농장인 , Hanja : 農丈人 , romanizado: Nongjangin ) é 1 "
"estrela ó suroeste da *Culler do Sur*."

#. Description of Korean constellation Dog
msgid "*Dog* (Korean: 구, Hanja: 狗, Romanization: Gu) consists of 2 stars."
msgstr "*Can* (en coreano: 구, en hanja: 狗, romanizado: Gu) ten 2 estrelas."

#. Description of Korean constellation Celestial Cock
msgid ""
"*Celestial Cock* (Korean: 천계, Hanja: 天雞, Romanization: Cheongye) consists of"
" 2 stars north of the *Territory of Dog*, west of the *Ox*."
msgstr ""
"O *Galo Celestial* (en coreano: 천계, en hanja: 天雞, romanizado: Cheongye) "
"consta de 2 estrelas ó norte do *Territorio do Can*, ó oeste do *Boi*."

#. Description of Korean constellation Territory of Dog
msgid ""
"Territory of Dog (Korean: 구국, Hanja: 狗國, Romanization: Guguk) consists of 4 "
"stars southeast of the *Establishment Stars*."
msgstr ""
"O Territorio do Can (en coreano: 구국, en hanja: 狗國, romanizado: Guguk) consta"
" de 4 estrelas ó sueste das *Estrelas do Establecemento*."

#. Description of Korean constellation River Turtle
msgid ""
"*River Turtle* (Korean: 별, Hanja: 鱉, Romanization: Byeol) consists of 14 "
"stars south of the *Dipper*."
msgstr ""
"*Tartaruga de río* (en coreano: 별, en hanja: 鱉, romanizado: Byeol) consta de"
" 14 estrelas ó sur da *Culler*."

#. Description of Korean constellation Celestial Spring
msgid ""
"*Celestial Spring* (Korean: 천연, Hanja: 天淵, Romanization: Cheonyeon) consists"
" of 10 stars southeast of the *River Turtle*, between the *River Turtle* and"
" the *Nine Water Wells*."
msgstr ""
"A *Fonte Celestial* (en coreano: 천연, en hanja: 天淵, romanizado: Cheonyeon) "
"consta de 10 estrelas ó sueste da *Tartaruga de Río*, entre a *Tartaruga de "
"Río* e os *Nove Pozos de Auga*."

#. Description of Korean constellation Leading Ox
msgid ""
"*Ox* (Korean: 견우, Hanja: 牽牛, Romanization: Gyeonu) consists of 6 stars."
msgstr ""
"*Boi* (en coreano: 견우, en hanja: 牽牛, romanizado: Gyeonu) consta de 6 "
"estrelas."

#. Description of Korean constellation Celestial Drumstick
msgid ""
"*Celestial Drumstick* (Korean: 천부, Hanja: 天桴, Romanization: Cheonbu) "
"consists of 4 stars lined horizontally north of the *Ox*."
msgstr ""
"*Baqueta celestial* (coreano: 천부, hanja: 天桴, romanizado: Cheonbu) consta de "
"4 estrelas aliñadas horizontalmente ó norte do *Boi*."

#. Description of Korean constellation Drum at the River
msgid ""
"*Drum at the River* (Korean: 하고, Hanja: 河鼓, Romanization: Hago) consists of "
"3 stars northwest of the *Ox*."
msgstr ""
"*Tambor no Río* (coreano: 하고, Hanja: 河鼓, romanizado: Hago) consta de 3 "
"estrelas ó noroeste do *Boi*."

#. Description of Korean constellation Right Flag
msgid ""
"*Right Flag* (Korean: 우기, Hanja: 右旗, Romanization: Ugi) consists of 9 stars "
"north of the *Ox*, southwest of the *Drum at the River*."
msgstr ""
"A *Bandeira Dereita* (en coreano: 우기, en hanja: 右旗, romanizado: Ugi) consta "
"de 9 estrelas ó norte do *Boi*, ó suroeste do *Tambor no Río*."

#. Description of Korean constellation Left Flag
msgid ""
"*Left Flag* (Korean: 좌기, Hanja: 左旗, Romanization: Jwagi) consists of 9 stars"
" beside the left of the *Drum at the River*."
msgstr ""
"A *Bandeira Esquerda* (en coreano: 좌기, en hanja: 左旗, romanizado Jwagi) "
"consta de 9 estrelas á esquerda do *Tambor no río*."

#. Description of Korean constellation Clepsydra Terrace
msgid ""
"*Clepsydra Terrace* (Korean: 점대, Hanja: 漸臺, Romanization: Jeomdae) consists "
"of 4 stars southeast of the *Weaving Girl*."
msgstr ""
"A *Terraza da Clepsidra* (en coreano: 점대, en hanja: 漸臺, romanizado: Jeomdae)"
" consta de 4 estrelas ó sueste da *Tecelá*."

#. Description of Korean constellation Imperial Passageway
msgid ""
"*Imperial Passageway* (Korean: 연도, Hanja: 輦道, Romanization: Yeondo) consists"
" of 5 stars northeast of the *Clepsydra Terrace*."
msgstr ""
"*Pasaxe Imperial* (coreano: 연도, Hanja: 輦道, romanización: Yeondo) consta de 5"
" estrelas ó nordeste da *Terraza da Clepsidra*."

#. Description of Korean constellation Weaving Girl
msgid ""
"*Weaving Girl* (Korean: 직녀, Hanja: 織女, Romanization: Jingnyeon) consists of "
"3 stars at the eastern end of the *Celestial Discipline*, northeast of the "
"*Heavenly Market Enclosure*."
msgstr ""
"*Teceá* (coreano: 직녀, hanja: 織女, romanizado: Jingnyeon) consta de 3 estrelas"
" no extremo leste da *Disciplina Celestial*, ó nordeste do *Recinto do "
"Mercado Celestial*."

#. Description of Korean constellation Network of Dykes
msgid ""
"*Network of Dykes* (Korean: 나언, Hanja: 羅堰, Romanization: Naeon) consists of "
"3 stars east of the *Ox*."
msgstr ""
"A *Rede de Diques* (en coreano: 나언, en hanja: 羅堰, romanizado: Naeon) consta "
"de 3 estrelas ó leste do *Boi*."

#. Description of Korean constellation Celestial Farmland (In Horn Mansion)
msgid ""
"*Celestial Farmland* (Korean: 천전, Hanja: 天田, Romanization: Cheonjeon) "
"consists of 9 stars south of the *Ox*."
msgstr ""
"*Terras de cultivo celestiais* (en coreano: 천전, en hanja: 天田, romanizado: "
"Cheonjeon) consta de 9 estrelas ó sur do *Boi*."

#. Description of Korean constellation Nine Water Wells
msgid ""
"*Nine Water Wells* (Korean: 구감, Hanja: 九坎, Romanization: Gugam) consists of "
"9 stars south of the *Ox*."
msgstr ""
"*Nove Pozos de Auga* (en coreano: 구감, en hanja: 九坎, romanizado: Gugam) "
"consta de 9 estrelas ó sur do *Boi*."

#. Description of Korean constellation Labor Woman
msgid ""
"*Girl* (Korean: 수녀, Hanja: 須女, Romanization: Sunyeo) consists of 4 stars."
msgstr ""
" *Rapariga* (en coreano: 수녀, en hanja: 須女, romanizado: Sunyeo) ten 4 "
"estrelas."

#. Description of Korean constellation Pearls on Ladies' Wear
msgid ""
"*Pearls on Ladies' Wear* (Korean: 이주, Hanja: 離珠, Romanization: Iju) consists"
" of 5 stars north of the *Girl*."
msgstr ""
"*Perlas nunha muller* (coreano: 이주, Hanja: 離珠, romanizado: Iju) consta de 5 "
"estrelas ónorte da *Rapariga*."

#. Description of Korean constellation Rotten Gourd
msgid ""
"*Rotten Gourd* (Korean: 패고, Hanja: 敗苽, Romanization: Paego) consists of 5 "
"stars beside the *Good Gourd*."
msgstr ""
"*Cabaza Podre* (coreano: 패고, hanja: 敗苽, romanizado: Paego) consta de 5 "
"estrelas onda *Cabaza Boa*."

#. Description of Korean constellation Good Gourd
msgid ""
"*Good Gourd* (Korean: 고, Hanja: 苽, Romanization: Go) consists of 5 stars "
"north of the *Pearls on Ladies' Wear*."
msgstr ""
"*Cabaza Boa* (coreano: 고, hanja: 苽, romanizado: Go) consta de 5 estrelas ó "
"norte das *Perlas nunha muller*."

#. Description of Korean constellation Celestial Ford
msgid ""
"*Celestial Ford* (Korean: 천진, Hanja: 天津, Romanization: Cheonjin) consists of"
" 9 stars in the milky way north of the *Good Gourd*."
msgstr ""
"*Vao Celestial* (coreano: 천진, hanja: 天津, romanizado: Cheonjin) consta de 9 "
"estrelas na Vía Láctea ó norte da *Cabaza Boa*."

#. Description of Korean constellation Xi Zhong
msgid ""
"*Xi Zhong* (Korean: 해중, Hanja: 奚仲, Romanization: Haejung) consists of 4 "
"stars, shaped like the *Railings* constellation, north of the *Celestial "
"Ford*."
msgstr ""
"*Xi Zhong* (en coreano: 해중, en hanja: 奚仲, romanizado: Haejung) consta de 4 "
"estrelas, coa forma da constelación das *Varandas*, situadas ó norte do *Vao"
" Celestial*."

#. Description of Korean constellation Basket for Mulberry Leaves
msgid ""
"Basket for Mulberry Leaves (Korean: 부광, Hanja: 扶筐, Romanization: Bugwang) "
"consists of 7 stars north of the Celestial Ford."
msgstr ""
"A Cesta para Follas de Moreira (en coreano: 부광, en hanja: 扶筐, romanizado: "
"Bugwang) consta de 7 estrelas ó norte do Vao Celestial."

#. Description of Korean constellation Twelve States
msgid ""
"*Twelve States* (Korean: 십이국, Hanja: 十二國, Romanization: Sibiguk) consists of"
" 16 stars."
msgstr ""
"*Doce Estados* (en coreano: 십이국, en hanja: 十二國, romanizado: Sibiguk) consta "
"de 16 estrelas."

#. Description of Korean constellation Yue State
msgid ""
"*Yue State* (Korean: 월, Hanja: 越, Romanization: Wol) is 1 star north of "
"*Zheng State*."
msgstr ""
"*Estado de Yue* (coreano: 월, Hanja: 越, romanizado: Wol) é 1 estrela ó norte "
"do *Estado de Zheng*."

#. Description of Korean constellation Zheng State
msgid ""
"*Zheng State* (Korean: 정, Hanja: 鄭, Romanization: Jeong) is 1 star north of "
"*Zhao State*."
msgstr ""
"O *Estado de Zheng* (en coreano: 정, en hanja: 鄭, romanizado: Jeong) está "
"situado a 1 estrela ó norte do *Estado de Zhao*."

#. Description of Korean constellation Zhao State
msgid ""
"*Zhao State* (Korean: 조, Hanja: 趙, Romanization: Jo) consists of 2 stars "
"north of *Qi State*."
msgstr ""
"O *Estado de Zhao* (en coreano: 조, en hanja: 趙, romanizado: Jo) consta de 2 "
"estrelas ó norte do *Estado de Qi*."

#. Description of Korean constellation Qi State
msgid ""
"*Qi State* (Korean: 제, Hanja: 齊, Romanization: Je) is 1 star east of the "
"*Nine Water Wells*."
msgstr ""
"O *Estado de Qi* (en coreano: 제, en hanja: 齊, romanizado: Je) está situado a"
" 1 estrela ó leste dos *Nove Pozos de Auga*."

#. Description of Korean constellation Zhou State
msgid ""
"*Zhou State* (Korean: 주, Hanja: 周, Romanization: Ju) consists of 2 stars "
"east of *Yue State*."
msgstr ""
"O *Estado de Zhou* (en coreano: 주, en hanja: 周, romanizado: Ju) consta de 2 "
"estrelas ó leste do *Estado de Yue*."

#. Description of Korean constellation Qin State
msgid ""
"*Qin State* (Korean: 진, Hanja: 秦, Romanization: Jin) consists of 2 stars, "
"lined north-south southeast of *Zhou*."
msgstr ""
"O *Estado de Qin* (en coreano: 진, en hanja: 秦, en romanizado: Jin) consta de"
" dúas estrelas, aliñadas de norte a sur e sueste de *Zhou*."

#. Description of Korean constellation Dai State
msgid ""
"*Dai State* (Korean: 대, Hanja: 代, Romanization: Dae) consists of 2 stars "
"south of *Qin State*."
msgstr ""
"O *estado de Dai* (en coreano: 대, en hanja: 代, romanizado: Dae) consta de 2 "
"estrelas ó sur do *Estado de Qin*."

#. Description of Korean constellation Jin State
msgid ""
"*Jin State* (Korean: 진, Hanja: 晉, Romanization: Jin) is 1 star west of *Dai "
"State*."
msgstr ""
"*Estado de Jin* (en coreano: 진, Hanja: 晉, romanizado: Jin) está situado a 1 "
"estrela ó norte do *Estado de Dai*."

#. Description of Korean constellation Han State
msgid ""
"*Han State* (Korean: 한, Hanja: 韓, Romanization: Han) is 1 star north of *Jin"
" State*."
msgstr ""
"O *Estado de Han* (en coreano: 한, en hanja: 韓, romanizado: Han) está situado"
" a 1 estrela ó norte do *Estado de Jin*."

#. Description of Korean constellation Wei State
msgid ""
"*Wei State* (Korean: 위, Hanja: 魏, Romanization: Wi) is 1 star north of *Han "
"State*."
msgstr ""
"*Estado de Wei* (coreano: 위, Hanja: 魏, romanizado: Wi) é 1 estrela ó norte "
"do *Estado de Han*."

#. Description of Korean constellation Chu State
msgid ""
"*Chu State* (Korean: 초, Hanja: 楚, Romanization: Cho) is 1 star west of *Wei "
"State*."
msgstr ""
"O *Estado de Chu* (en coreano: 초, en hanja: 楚, romanizado: Cho) está situado"
" a 1 estrela ó oeste do *Estado de Wei*."

#. Description of Korean constellation Yan State
msgid ""
"*Yan State* (Korean: 연, Hanja: 燕, Romanization: Yeon) is 1 star south of "
"*Chu State*."
msgstr ""
"O *Estado de Yan* (en coreano: 연, en hanja: 燕, romanizado: Yeon) está "
"situado a 1 estrela ó sur do *Estado de Chu*."

#. Description of Korean constellation Emptiness
msgid ""
"*Emptiness* (Korean: 허, Hanja: 虛, Romanization: Heo) consists of 2 stars."
msgstr ""
"*Baleiro* (coreano: 허, Hanja: 虛, romanizado: Heo) consta de 2 estrelas."

#. Description of Korean constellation Deified Judge of Life
msgid ""
"*Deified Judge of Life* (Korean: 사명, Hanja: 司命, Romanization: Samyeong) "
"consists of 2 stars north of the *Emptiness*."
msgstr ""
"*Xuíz Deificado da Vida* (en coreano: 사명, en hanja: 司命, romanizado: "
"Samyeong) consta de 2 estrelas ó norte do *Baleiro*."

#. Description of Korean constellation Deified Judge of Rank
msgid ""
"*Deified Judge of Rank* (Korean: 사록, Hanja: 司祿, Romanization: Sarok) "
"consists of 2 stars north of the *Deified Judge of Life*."
msgstr ""
"*Xuíz de Rango Deificado* (coreano: 사록, hanja: 司祿, romanizado: Sarok) consta"
" de 2 estrelas ó norte do *Xuíz de Vida Deificado*."

#. Description of Korean constellation Deified Judge of Disaster and Good
#. Fortune
msgid ""
"*Deified Judge of Disaster and Good Fortune* (Korean: 사위, Hanja: 司危, "
"Romanization: Sawi) consists of 2 stars north of the *Deified Judge of "
"Rank*."
msgstr ""
"*Xuíz Deificado do Desastre e da Boa Fortuna* (en coreano: 사위, en hanja: 司危,"
" romanizado: Sawi) consta de 2 estrelas ó norte do *Xuíz de Rango "
"Deificado*."

#. Description of Korean constellation Deified Judge of Right and Wrong
msgid ""
"*Deified Judge of Right and Wrong* (Korean: 사비, Hanja: 司非, Romanization: "
"Sabi) consists of 2 stars north of the *Deified Judge of Disaster and Good "
"Fortune*."
msgstr ""
"*Xuíz Divinizado do Ben e do Mal* (en coreano: 사비, en hanja: 司非, romanizado:"
" Sabi) consta de 2 estrelas ó norte do *Xuíz Deificado do Desastre e da Boa "
"Fortuna*."

#. Description of Korean constellation Crying
msgid ""
"*Crying* (Korean: 곡, Hanja: 哭, Romanization: Gok) consists of 2 stars south "
"of the *Emptiness*."
msgstr ""
"*Choro* (coreano: 곡, hanja: 哭, romanizado: Gok) consta de 2 estrelas ó sur "
"do *Baleiro*."

#. Description of Korean constellation Weeping
msgid ""
"*Weeping* (Korean: 읍, Hanja: 泣, Romanization: Eup) consists of 2 stars east "
"of the *Crying*."
msgstr ""
"*Pranto* (coreano: 읍, hanja: 泣, romanizado: Eup) consta de 2 estrelas ó "
"leste de *Choro*."

#. Description of Korean constellation Celestial Ramparts
msgid ""
"*Celestial Ramparts* (Korean: 천루성, Hanja: 天壘城, Romanization: Cheolluseong) "
"consists of 12 stars south of the *Crying* and *Weeping*."
msgstr ""
"*Varandas Celestes* (en coreano: 천루성, en hanja: 天壘城, romanizado: "
"Cheolluseong) consta de 12 estrelas ó sur das *Choro* e *Pranto*."

#. Description of Korean constellation Decayed Mortar
msgid ""
"*Decayed Mortar* (Korean: 패구, Hanja: 敗臼, Romanization: Paegu) consists of 4 "
"stars south of the *Emptiness* and *Rooftop*."
msgstr ""
"*Mortero Deteriorado* (en coreano: 패구, en hanja: 敗臼, romanizado: Paegu) "
"consta de 4 estrelas ó sur do *Baleiro* e da *Azotea*."

#. Description of Korean constellation Jade Ornament on Ladies' Wear
msgid ""
"*Jade Ornament on Ladies' Wear* (Korean: 이유, Hanja: 離瑜, Romanization: Iyu) "
"consists of 3 stars, lined north-south southeast of *Qin State* and *Dai "
"State*."
msgstr ""
"*Ornamento de Xade nunha Muller* (coreano: 이유, hanja: 離瑜, romanizado: Iyu) "
"consta de 3 estrelas, aliñadas de norte a sur e sueste entre o *Estado de "
"Qin* e o *Estado de Dai*."

#. Description of Korean constellation Rooftop
msgid ""
"*Rooftop* (Korean: 위, Hanja: 危, Romanization: Wi) consists of 3 stars "
"southeast of the *Celestial Ford*."
msgstr ""
"*Azotea* (coreano: 위, hanja: 危, romanizadon: Wi) consta de 3 estrelas ó "
"sueste do *Vao Celestial*."

#. Description of Korean constellation Tomb (Vassal of Rooftop)
msgid ""
"*Tomb* (Korean: 분묘, Hanja: 墳墓, Romanization: Bunmyo) consists of 4 stars "
"south of the *Rooftop*."
msgstr ""
"*Tumba* (coreano: 분묘, hanja: 墳墓, romanizado: Bunmyo) consta de 4 ó sur da "
"*Azotea*."

#. Description of Korean constellation Humans Stars
msgid ""
"*Humans Stars* (Korean: 인성, Hanja: 人星, Romanization: Inseong) consists of 5 "
"stars southeast of the *Big Yard for Chariots*, north of the *Emptiness*."
msgstr ""
"*Estrelas Humanas* (coreano: 인성, hanja: 人星, romanizado: Inseong) consta de 5"
" estrelas ó sueste do *Gran Patio de Carros*, ó norte do *Baleiro*."

#. Description of Korean constellation Inner Pestle
msgid ""
"*Pestle* (Korean: 내저, Hanja: 內杵, Romanization: Naejeo) consists of 3 stars "
"east of the *Humans Stars*, beside the milky way."
msgstr ""
"*Pailán* (corean: 내저, hanja: 內杵, romanizado: Naejeo) consta de 3 estrelas ó "
"leste das *Estrelas Humanas*, onda a Vía Láctea."

#. Description of Korean constellation Mortar
msgid ""
"*Mortar* (Korean: 구, Hanja: 臼, Romanization: Gu) consists of 4 stars east of"
" the *Humans Stars*, under the *Pestle* stars."
msgstr ""
"*Morteiro* (coreano: 구, hanja: 臼, romanizado: Gu) consta de 4 estrelas ó "
"leste das *Estrelas Humanas*, baixo as estrelas *Pailián*."

#. Description of Korean constellation Big Yard for Chariots
msgid ""
"*Big Yard for Chariots* (Korean: 차부, Hanja: 車府, Romanization: Chabu) "
"consists of 7 stars east of the *Celestial Ford*, near the milky way, lined "
"east-west."
msgstr ""
"O *Gran Patio de Carros* (en coreano: 차부, en hanja: 車府, romanizado: Chabu) "
"consta de 7 estrelas ó leste do *Vao Celestial*, preto da Vía Láctea, "
"aliñadas de leste a oeste."

#. Description of Korean constellation Zaofu
msgid ""
"*Zaofu* (Korean: 조부, Hanja: 造父, Romanization: Jobu) consists of 5 stars "
"south of the *Celestial Hook*, in the milky way."
msgstr ""
"*Zaofu* (en coreano: 조부, en hanja: 造父, romanizado: Jobu) consta de 5 "
"estrelas ó sur do *Gancho Celestial*, na Vía Láctea."

#. Description of Korean constellation Hook
msgid ""
"*Celestial Hook* (Korean: 구, Hanja: 鈎, Romanization: Gu) consists of 9 stars"
" north of *Zaofu*."
msgstr ""
"*Gancho Celestial* (en coreano: 구, en hanja: 鈎, romanizado: Gu) consta de 9 "
"estrelas ó norte de *Zaofu*."

#. Description of Korean constellation Roofing
msgid ""
"*Roofing* (Korean: 개옥, Hanja: 蓋屋, Romanization: Gaeok) consists of 2 stars "
"south of the *Rooftop*."
msgstr ""
"*Teito* (coreano: 개옥, hanja: 蓋屋, romanizado: gaeok) consta de 2 estrelas ó "
"sur da *Azotea*."

#. Description of Korean constellation Temple
msgid ""
"*Temple* (Korean: 허량, Hanja: 虛梁, Romanization: Heoryang) consists of 4 stars"
" south of the *Rooftop*."
msgstr ""
"O *Templo* (en coreano: 허량, en hanja: 虛梁, romanizado: Heoryang) consta de 4 "
"estrelas ó sur da *Azotea*."

#. Description of Korean constellation Celestial Money
msgid ""
"*Celestial Money* (Korean: 천전, Hanja: 天錢, Romanization: Cheonjeon) consists "
"of 10 stars northwest of the *North Gate of the Military Camp*."
msgstr ""
"O *Diñeiro Celestial* (en coreano: 천전, en hanja: 天錢, romanizado: Cheonjeon) "
"consta de 10 estrelas ó noroeste da *Porta Norte do Campamento Militar*."

#. Description of Korean constellation Encampment
msgid ""
"*Encampment* (Korean: 실, Hanja: 室, Romanization: Sil) consists of 2 stars."
msgstr ""
"*Campamento* (en coreano: 실, en hanja: 室, en romanizado: Sil) consta de 2 "
"estrelas."

#. Description of Korean constellation Resting Palace (Vassal of Encampment)
msgid ""
"*Resting Palace* (Korean: 이궁, Hanja: 離宮, Romanization: Igung) consists of 6 "
"stars."
msgstr ""
"O *Palacio de Descanso* (en coreano: 이궁, en hanja: 離宮, romanizado: Igung) "
"ten 6 estrelas."

#. Description of Korean constellation Flying Serpent
msgid ""
"*Flying Serpent* (Korean: 등사, Hanja: 騰蛇, Romanization: Deungsa) consists of "
"22 stars north of the *Encampment*."
msgstr ""
"A *Serpe Voadora* (en coreano: 등사, en hanja: 騰蛇, romanizado: Deungsa) consta"
" de 22 estrelas ó norte do *Campamento*."

#. Description of Korean constellation Thunder and Lightning
msgid ""
"*Thunder and Lightning* (Korean: 뇌전, Hanja: 雷電, Romanization: Noejeon) "
"consists of 6 stars southwest of the *Encampment*."
msgstr ""
"*Trono e Lóstrego* (en coreano: 뇌전, en hanja: 雷電, romanizado: Noejeon) "
"consta de 6 estrelas ó suroeste do *Campamento*."

#. Description of Korean constellation Official for Materials Supply
msgid ""
"*Official for Materials Supply* (Korean: 토공리, Hanja: 土公吏, Romanization: "
"Togongni) consists of 2 stars southwest of the *Encampment*."
msgstr ""
"*Oficial de Subministración de Materiais* (coreano: 토공리, Hanja: 土公吏, "
"romanizado: Togongni) consta de 2 estrelas ó suroeste do *Campamento*."

#. Description of Korean constellation Palace Guard
msgid ""
"*Palace Guard* (Korean: 우림군, Hanja: 羽林軍, Romanization: Urimgun) consists of "
"45 stars south of the Encampment, south of the *Line of Ramparts*."
msgstr ""
"A *Garda do Palacio* (en coreano: 우림군, en hanja: 羽林軍, romanizadoi: Urimgun) "
"consta de 45 estrelas ó sur do Campamento, ó sur da *Liña de Murallas*."

#. Description of Korean constellation Line of Ramparts
msgid ""
"*Line of Ramparts* (Korean: 누벽진, Hanja: 壘壁陣, Romanization: Nubyeokjin) "
"consists of 12 stars south of the *Encampment* and *Wall*, north of the "
"*Palace Guard*."
msgstr ""
"A *Liña de Murallas* (en coreano: 누벽진, en hanja: 壘壁陣, romanizado: "
"Nubyeokjin) consta de 12 estrelas ó sur do *Campamento* e da *Muralla*, e ó "
"norte da *Garda do Palacio*."

#. Description of Korean constellation Axe
msgid ""
"*Axe* (Korean: 부월, Hanja: 鈇鉞, Romanization: Buwol) consists of 3 stars east "
"of the *North Gate of the Military Camp*."
msgstr ""
"*Machada* (en coreano: 부월, en hanja: 鈇鉞, romanizado: Buwol) consta de 3 "
"estrelas ó leste da *Porta Norte do Campamento Militar*."

#. Description of Korean constellation North Gate of the Military Camp
msgid ""
"*North Gate of the Military Camp* (Korean: 북락사문, Hanja: 北落師門, Romanization: "
"Bungnaksamun) is 1 star southwest of the *Palace Guard*."
msgstr ""
"*Porta Norte do Campamento Militar* (coreano: 북락사문, Hanja: 北落師門, romanizado:"
" Bungnaksamun) é 1 estrela ó suroeste da *Garda do Palacio*."

#. Description of Korean constellation Materials for Making Tents
msgid ""
"*Materials for Making Tents* (Korean: 천강, Hanja: 天綱, Romanization: "
"Cheongang) is 1 star southwest of the *North Gate of the Military Camp*."
msgstr ""
"*Materiais para Facer Tendas* (en coreano: 천강, en hanja: 天綱, romanizado: "
"Cheongang) está a 1 estrela ó suroeste da *Porta Norte do Campamento "
"Militar*."

#. Description of Korean constellation Net for Catching Birds
msgid ""
"*Net for Catching Birds* (Korean: 팔괴, Hanja: 八魁, Romanization: Palgwae) "
"consists of 9 stars southeast of the *North Gate of the Military Camp*."
msgstr ""
"A *Rede para Cazar Paxaros* (en coreano: 팔괴, en hanja: 八魁, romanizado: "
"Palgwae) consta de 9 estrelas ó sueste da *Porta Norte do Campamento "
"Militar*."

#. Description of Korean constellation Eastern Wall
msgid ""
"*Wall* (Korean: 동벽, Hanja: 東壁, Romanization: Dongbyeok) consists of 2 stars."
msgstr ""
"*Muro* (en coreano: 동벽, en hanja: 東壁, romanizado: Dongbyeok) ten 2 estrelas."

#. Description of Korean constellation Celestial Stable
msgid ""
"*Celestial Stable* (Korean: 천구, Hanja: 天厩, Romanization: Cheongu) consists "
"of 10 stars north of the *Wall*, near *Wang Liang*."
msgstr ""
"O *Cortello Celestial* (en coreano: 천구, en hanja: 天厩, romanizado: Cheongu) "
"consta de 10 estrelas ónorte do *Murro*, preto de *Wang Liang*."

#. Description of Korean constellation Official for Earthworks and Buildings
msgid ""
"*Official for Earthworks and Buildings* (Korean: 토공, Hanja: 土公, "
"Romanization: Togong) consists of 2 stars south of the *Wall*."
msgstr ""
"*Oficial para Movementos de Terras e Edificios* (en coreano: 토공, en hanja: "
"土公, en romanizado: Togong) consta de 2 estrelas ó sur do *Muro*."

#. Description of Korean constellation Thunderbolt
msgid ""
"*Thunderbolt* (Korean: 벽력, Hanja: 霹靂, Romanization: Byeongnyeok) consists of"
" 5 stars southwest of the *Official for Earthworks and Buildings*, north of "
"the *Cloud and Rain*."
msgstr ""
"*Lóstrego* (coreano: 벽력, hanja: 霹靂, romanizado: Byeongnyeok) consta de 5 "
"estrelas ó suroeste do *Oficial de Movementos de Terras e Edificios*, ó "
"norte de *Nube e Choiva*."

#. Description of Korean constellation Cloud and Rain
msgid ""
"*Cloud and Rain* (Korean: 운우, Hanja: 雲雨, Romanization: Unu) consists of 4 "
"stars south of the *Thunderbolt*, east of the *Thunder and Lightning*."
msgstr ""
"*Nube e Choiva* (coreano: 운우, Hanja: 雲雨, romanizado: Unu) consta de 4 "
"estrelas ó sur do *Lóstrego*, ó leste do *Trono e Lóstrego*."

#. Description of Korean constellation Sickle
msgid ""
"*Sickle* (Korean: 부질, Hanja: 鈇鑕, Romanization: Bujil) consists of 5 stars "
"southwest of the *Square Celestial Granary*."
msgstr ""
"*Fouce* (en coreano: 부질, en hanja: 鈇鑕, romanizado: Bujil) consta de 5 "
"estrelas ó suroeste do *Celeiro Cadrado*."

#. Description of Korean constellation Legs
msgid "*Legs* (Korean: 규, Hanja: 奎, Romanization: Gyu) consists of 16 stars."
msgstr ""
"*Pernas* (en coreano: 규, en hanja: 奎, romanizado: Gyu) consta de 16 "
"estrelas."

#. Description of Korean constellation Auxiliary Road
msgid ""
"*Auxiliary Road* (Korean: 부로, Hanja: 附路, Romanization: Buro) is 1 star "
"beside the south of the *Flying Corridor*, east of *Wang Liang*."
msgstr ""
"*Vía Auxiliar* (coreano: 부로, Hanja: 附路, romanizado: Buro) é 1 estrela ó lado"
" do sur do *Flying Corredor*, ó leste de *Wang Liang*."

#. Description of Korean constellation Flying Corridor
msgid ""
"*Flying Corridor* (Korean: 각도, Hanja: 閣道, Romanization: Gakdo) consists of 6"
" stars in front of *Wang Liang*."
msgstr ""
"O *Corredor Voador* (en coreano: 각도, en hanja: 閣道, romanizadon: Gakdo) "
"consta de 6 estrelas diante de *Wang Liang*."

#. Description of Korean constellation Wang Liang
msgid ""
"*Wang Liang* (Korean: 왕량, Hanja: 王良, Romanization: Wangnyang) consists of 5 "
"stars in the river north of the *Legs*."
msgstr ""
"*Wang Liang* (coreano: 왕량, Hanja: 王良, romanizado: Wangnyang) consta de 5 "
"estrelas no río ó norte das *Pernas*."

#. Description of Korean constellation Whip
msgid ""
"*Whip* (Korean: 책, Hanja: 策, Romanization: Chaek) is 1 star north of *Wang "
"Liang*."
msgstr ""
"*Tralla* (en coreano: 책, en hanja: 策, romanizado: Chaek) está situado a 1 "
"estrela ó norte de *Wang Liang*."

#. Description of Korean constellation Southern Military Gate
msgid ""
"*Southern Military Gate* (Korean: 군남문, Hanja: 軍南門, Romanization: Gunnam Mun)"
" is 1 star southwest of the *Great General of Heaven*."
msgstr ""
"A *Porta Militar do Sur* (en coreano: 군남문, en hanja: 軍南門, romanizado: Gunnam"
" Mun) está situada a 1 estrela ó suroeste do *Gran Xeneral do Ceo*."

#. Description of Korean constellation Outer Fence
msgid ""
"*Outer Fence* (Korean: 외병, Hanja: 外屏, Romanization: Oebyeong) consists of 7 "
"stars south of the *Legs*."
msgstr ""
"*Valado Exterior* (en coreano: 외병, en hanja: 外屏, romanizado: Oebyeong) "
"consta de 7 estrelas ó sur das *Pernas*."

#. Description of Korean constellation Celestial Pigsty
msgid ""
"*Celestial Pigsty* (Korean: 천혼, Hanja: 天溷, Romanization: Cheonhon) consists "
"of 7 stars south of the *Outer Screen*."
msgstr ""
"*Porqueira Celestial* (en coreano: 천혼, en hanja: 天溷, romanizado: Cheonhon) "
"consta de 7 estrelas ó sur da *Pantalla Exterior*."

#. Description of Korean constellation Master of Constructions (In Legs
#. Mansion)
msgid ""
"*Master of Constructions* (Korean: 토사공, Hanja: 司空, Romanization: Sagong) is "
"1 star south of the *Legs*."
msgstr ""
"*Mestre de Construcións* (en coreano: 토사공, en hanja: 司空, romanizado: Sagong)"
" está a 1 estrela ó sur das *Pernas*."

#. Description of Korean constellation Bond
msgid "*Bond* (Korean: 루, Hanja: 婁, Romanization: Ru) consists of 3 stars."
msgstr ""
"*Ligazón* (en coreano: 루, en hanja: 婁, romanizado: Ru) ten 3 estrelas."

#. Description of Korean constellation General of Heaven
msgid ""
"*Great General of Heaven* (Korean: 천장군, Hanja: 天將軍, Romanization: "
"Cheonganggun) consists of 11 stars north of the *Bond*."
msgstr ""
"O *Gran Xeneral do Ceo* (en coreano: 천장군, en hanja: 天將軍, romanizado: "
"Cheonganggun) consta de 11 estrelas ó norte de *Ligazón*."

#. Description of Korean constellation Official in Charge of Pasturing
msgid ""
"*Official in Charge of Pasturing* (Korean: 우경, Hanja: 右更, Romanization: "
"Ugyeong) consists of 5 stars west of the *Bond*."
msgstr ""
"O *Funcionario Encargado do Pastoreo* (en coreano: 우경, en hanja: 右更, "
"romanizado: Ugyeong) consta de 5 estrelas ó oeste de *Ligazón*."

#. Description of Korean constellation Official in Charge of the Forest
msgid ""
"*Official in Charge of the Forest* (Korean: 좌경, Hanja: 左更, Romanization: "
"Jwagyeong) consists of 5 stars east of the *Bond*."
msgstr ""
"*Funcionario a Cargo do Bosque* (en coreano: 좌경, en hanja: 左更, romanizado: "
"Jwagyeong) consta de 5 estrelas ó leste de *Ligazón*."

#. Description of Korean constellation Square Celestial Granary
msgid ""
"*Square Celestial Granary* (Korean: 천창, Hanja: 天倉, Romanization: Cheonchang)"
" consists of 6 stars south of the *Bond*."
msgstr ""
"O *Celeiro Celestial Cadrado* (en coreano: 천창, en hanja: 天倉, romanizado: "
"Cheonchang) consta de 6 estrelas ósur de *Ligazón*."

#. Description of Korean constellation Ricks of Grain
msgid ""
"*Ricks of Grain* (Korean: 천유, Hanja: 天庾, Romanization: Cheonyu) consists of "
"3 stars southeast of the *Square Celestial Granary*."
msgstr ""
"*Moreas de Gran* (en coreano: 천유, en hanja: 天庾, romanizado: Cheonyu) consta "
"de 3 estrelas ó sueste do *Celeiro Cadrado Celestial*."

#. Description of Korean constellation Stomach
msgid "*Stomach* (Korean: 위, Hanja: 胃, Romanization: Wi) consists of 3 stars."
msgstr ""
"*Estómago* (en coreano: 위, en hanja: 胃, romanizado: Wi) ten 3 estrelas."

#. Description of Korean constellation Mausoleum
msgid ""
"*Mausoleum* (Korean: 대릉, Hanja: 大陵, Romanization: Daereung) consists of 8 "
"stars north of the *Stomach*."
msgstr ""
"O *Mausoleo* (en coreano: 대릉, en hanja: 大陵, romanizado: Daereung) consta de "
"8 estrelas ó norte do *Estómago*."

#. Description of Korean constellation Heap of Corpses (In Stomach Mansion)
msgid ""
"*Heap of Corpses* (Korean: 적시, Hanja: 積尸, Romanization: Jeoksi) is 1 star in"
" the *Mausoleum*."
msgstr ""
"*Morea de cadáveres* (en coreano: 적시, en hanja: 積尸, romanizado: Jeoksi) é "
"unha estrela do *Mausoleo*."

#. Description of Korean constellation Celestial Boat
msgid ""
"*Celestial Boat* (Korean: 천선, Hanja: 天船, Romanization: Cheonseon) consists "
"of 9 stars north of the *Mausoleum*, in the milky way."
msgstr ""
"*Barco Celestial* (coreano: 천선, Hanja: 天船, romanizado: Cheonseon) consta de "
"9 estrelas ó norte do *Mausoleo*, na vía láctea."

#. Description of Korean constellation Stored water (In Stomach Mansion)
msgid ""
"*Stored water* (Korean: 적수, Hanja: 積水, Romanization: Jeoksu) is 1 star in "
"the *Celestial Boat*."
msgstr ""
"*Auga Almacenada* (en coreano: 적수, en hanja: 積水, romanizado: Jeoksu) é 1 "
"estrela no *Barco Celestial*."

#. Description of Korean constellation Circular Celestial Granary
msgid ""
"*Circular Celestial Granary* (Korean: 천균, Hanja: 天囷, Romanization: "
"Cheongyun) consists of 13 stars south of the *Stomach*, shaped like a "
"character \"乙\"."
msgstr ""
"*Celeiro Cricular Celestial* (coreano: 천균, Hanja: 天囷, romanizado: Cheongyun)"
" consta de 13 estrelas ó sur do *Estómago*, con forma de carácter \"乙\"."

#. Description of Korean constellation Celestial Foodstuff
msgid ""
"*Celestial Foodstuff* (Korean: 천름, Hanja: 天廩, Romanization: Cheolleum) "
"consists of 4 stars south of the *Hairy Head*."
msgstr ""
"*Comida celestial* (en coreano: 천름, en hanja: 天廩, romanizado: Cheolleum) "
"consta de 4 estrelas ó sur da *Cabeza Peluda*."

#. Description of Korean constellation Hairy Head
msgid ""
"*Hairy Head* (Korean: 묘, Hanja: 昴, Romanization: Myo) consists of 7 stars."
msgstr ""
"*Cabeza Peluda* (en coreano: 묘, en hanja: 昴, romanizado: Myo) ten 7 "
"estrelas."

#. Description of Korean constellation Celestial Concave
msgid ""
"*Celestial Concave* (Korean: 천아, Hanja: 天阿, Romanization: Cheon-a) is 1 star"
" northwest of the *Hairy Head*."
msgstr ""
"*Cóncavo Celestial* (en coreano: 천아, en hanja: 天阿, romanizado: Cheon-a) está"
" situado a 1 estrela ó noroeste da *Cabeza Peluda*."

#. Description of Korean constellation Rolled Tongue
msgid ""
"*Rolled Tongue* (Korean: 권설, Hanja: 卷舌, Romanization: Gwonseol) consists of "
"6 stars north of the *Hairy Head*."
msgstr ""
"*Lingua Enrolada* (en coreano: 권설, en hanja: 卷舌, romanizado: Gwonseol) "
"consta de 6 estrelas ó norte da *Cabeza Peluda*."

#. Description of Korean constellation Celestial Slander
msgid ""
"*Celestial Slander* (Korean: 천참, Hanja: 天讒, Romanization: Cheoncham) is 1 "
"star in the *Rolled Tongue*."
msgstr ""
"*Calumnia Celestial* (coreano: 천참, Hanja: 天讒, romanizado: Cheoncham) é 1 "
"estrela na *Lingua Enrolada*."

#. Description of Korean constellation Whetstone
msgid ""
"*Whetstone* (Korean: 려석, Hanja: 礪石, Romanization: Ryeoseok) consists of 4 "
"stars southeast of the *Rolled Tongue*."
msgstr ""
"*Pedra de afiar* (en coreano: 려석, en hanja: 礪石, romanizado: Ryeoseok) consta"
" de 4 estrelas ósueste da *Lingua Enrolada*."

#. Description of Korean constellation Lunar Star
msgid ""
"*Lunar Star* (Korean: 월, Hanja: 月, Romanization: Wol) is 1 star east of the "
"*Hairy Head*."
msgstr ""
"A *Estrela Lunar* (en coreano: 월, en hanja: 月, romanizado: Wol) está situada"
" 1 estrela ó leste da *Cabeza Peluda*."

#. Description of Korean constellation Celestial Yin Force
msgid ""
"*Celestial Yin Force* (Korean: 천음, Hanja: 天陰, Romanization: Cheon-eum) "
"consists of 5 stars west of the *Net*'s handle."
msgstr ""
"A *Forza Yin Celestial* (en coreano: 천음, en hanja: 天陰, romanizado: Cheon-"
"eum) consta de 5 estrelas óoeste do identificador de *Rede*."

#. Description of Korean constellation Hay
msgid ""
"*Hay* (Korean: 추고, Hanja: 芻藁, Romanization: Chugo) consists of 6 stars west "
"of the *Celestial Meadows*."
msgstr ""
"*Feno* (en coreano: 추고, en hanja: 芻藁, romanizado: Chugo) consta de 6 "
"estrelas ó oeste dos *Prados Celestes*."

#. Description of Korean constellation Celestial Meadows
msgid ""
"*Celestial Meadows* (Korean: 천원, Hanja: 天苑, Romanization: Cheon-won) "
"consists of 16 stars south of the *Net*."
msgstr ""
"*Praderías Celestiais* (en coreano: 천원, en hanja: 天苑, romanizado: Cheon-won)"
" constan de 16 estrelas ó sur da *Rede*."

#. Description of Korean constellation Net
msgid "*Net* (Korean: 필, Hanja: 畢, Romanization: Pil) consists of 8 stars."
msgstr ""
"*Rede* (en coreano: 필, en hanja: 畢, romanizado: Pil) consta de 8 estrelas."

#. Description of Korean constellation Whisper (Vassal of Net)
msgid ""
"*Whisper* (Korean: 부이, Hanja: 附耳, Romanization: Bui) is 1 star under the "
"*Net*."
msgstr ""
"*Susurro* (en coreano: 부이, en hanja: 附耳, romanizado: Bui) ten unha estrela "
"por debaixo da *Rede*."

#. Description of Korean constellation Celestial Street
msgid ""
"*Celestial Street* (Korean: 천가, Hanja: 天街, Romanization: Cheonga) consists "
"of 2 stars between the *Hairy Head* and *Net*, near the east of the *Lunar "
"Star*."
msgstr ""
"A *Rúa Celestial* (en coreano: 천가, en hanja: 天街, romanizado: Cheonga) consta"
" de dúas estrelas entre a *Cabeza Peluda* e a *Rede*, preto do leste da "
"*Estrela Lunar*."

#. Description of Korean constellation Feudal Kings
msgid ""
"*Feudal Kings* (Korean: 제왕, Hanja: 諸王, Romanization: Jewang) consists of 6 "
"stars south of the *Five Chariots*."
msgstr ""
"*Reis Feudais* (en coreano: 제왕, en hanja: 諸王, romanizado: Jewang) consta de "
"6 estrelas ó sur dos *Cinco Carros*."

#. Description of Korean constellation Celestial High Terrace
msgid ""
"*Celestial High Terrace* (Korean: 천고, Hanja: 天高, Romanization: Cheongo) "
"consists of 4 stars west of the *Banner of Three Stars*, near the *Net*."
msgstr ""
"A *Terraza Celestial Alta* (en coreano: 천고, en hanja: 天高, romanizado: "
"Cheongo) consta de 4 estrelas ó oeste da *Bandera das Tres Estrelas*, preto "
"da *Rede*."

#. Description of Korean constellation Five Chariots
msgid ""
"*Five Chariots* (Korean: 오거, Hanja: 五車, Romanization: Ogeo) consists of 5 "
"stars northeast of the *Net*."
msgstr ""
"*Cinco Carros* (en coreano: 오거, en hanja: 五車, romanizado: Ogeo) consta de 5 "
"estrelas ó nordeste da *Rede*."

#. Description of Korean constellation Pillars (In Net Mansion)
msgid ""
"*Pillars* (Korean: 주, Hanja: 柱, Romanization: Ju) consists of 9 stars "
"northeast of the *Net*."
msgstr ""
"*Piares* (en coreano: 주, en hanja: 柱, romanizado: Ju) consta de 9 estrelas ó"
" nordeste da *Rede*."

#. Description of Korean constellation Celestial Pier
msgid ""
"*Celestial Pier* (Korean: 천황, Hanja: 天潢, Romanization: Cheonhwang) consists "
"of 5 stars in the *Five Chariots*."
msgstr ""
"O *Peirao Celestial* (en coreano: 천황, en hanja: 天潢, romanizado: Cheonhwang) "
"consta de 5 estrelas nos *Cinco Carros*."

#. Description of Korean constellation Pool of Harmony
msgid ""
"*Pool of Harmony* (Korean: 함지, Hanja: 咸池, Romanization: Hamji) consists of 3"
" stars northwest of the *Celestial Pier*."
msgstr ""
"*Estanque da Harmonía* (en coreano: 함지, en hanja: 咸池, romanizado: Hamji) "
"consta de 3 estrelas ó noroeste do *Peirao Celestial*."

#. Description of Korean constellation Celestial Pass
msgid ""
"*Celestial Pass* (Korean: 천관, Hanja: 天關, Romanization: Cheongwan) is 1 star "
"south of the *Five Chariots*, northwest of the *Three Stars*."
msgstr ""
"O *Paso Celestial* (en coreano: 천관, en hanja: 天關, romanizado: Cheongwan) "
"está situado a 1 estrela ó sur dos *Cinco Carros* e ó noroeste das *Tres "
"Estrelas*."

#. Description of Korean constellation Celestial Tally
msgid ""
"*Celestial Tally* (Korean: 천절, Hanja: 天節, Romanization: Cheonjeol) consists "
"of 8 stars south of the *Net* and *Whisper*."
msgstr ""
"*Conta celestial* (en coreano: 천절, en hanja: 天節, romanizado: Cheonjeol) "
"consta de 8 estrelas ó sur da *Rede* e do *Susurro*."

#. Description of Korean constellation Interpreters of Nine Dialects
msgid ""
"*Interpreters of Nine Dialects* (Korean: 구주수구, Hanja: 九州殊口, Romanization: "
"Gujusugu) consists of 9 stars under the *Celestial Tally*."
msgstr ""
"*Intérpretes de nove dialectos* (coreano: 구주수구, hanja: 九州殊口, romanizado: "
"Gujusugu) consta de 9 estrelas baixo o *Conta Celestial*."

#. Description of Korean constellation Banner of Three Stars
msgid ""
"*Banner of Three Stars* (Korean: 삼기, Hanja: 參旗, Romanization: Samgi) "
"consists of 9 stars west of the *Three Stars*."
msgstr ""
"O *Estandarte das Tres Estrelas* (en coreano: 삼기, en hanja: 參旗, romanizado: "
"Samgi) consta de 9 estrelas ó oeste das *Tres Estrelas*."

#. Description of Korean constellation Imperial Military Flag
msgid ""
"*Imperial Military Flag* (Korean: 구유, Hanja: 九斿, Romanization: Guyu) "
"consists of 9 stars southwest of the *Jade Well*."
msgstr ""
"A *Bandeira Militar Imperial* (en coreano: 구유, en hanja: 九斿, romanizado: "
"Guyu) consta de 9 estrelas ío suroeste do *Pozo de Xade*."

#. Description of Korean constellation Celestial Orchard
msgid ""
"*Celestial Orchard* (Korean: 천원, Hanja: 天園, Romanization: Cheon-won) "
"consists of 13 stars south of the *Celestial Meadows*."
msgstr ""
"*Pomar Celestial* (en coreano: 천원, en hanja: 天園, romanizado: Cheon-won) "
"consta de 13 estrelas ó sur das *Praderías Celestiais*."

#. Description of Korean constellation Turtle Beak
msgid ""
"*Turtle Beak* (Korean: 자, Hanja: 觜, Romanization: Ja) consists of 3 stars."
msgstr ""
"*Peteiro de tartaruga* (en coreano: 자, en hanja: 觜, romanizado: Ja) ten 3 "
"estrelas."

#. Description of Korean constellation Deity in Charge of Monsters
msgid ""
"*Deity in Charge of Monsters* (Korean: 사괴, Hanja: 司恠, Romanization: Sagwae) "
"consists of 4 stars in front of the *Well* and the *Battle Axe*."
msgstr ""
"A *Deidade Encargada dos Monstros* (en coreano: 사괴, en hanja: 司恠, "
"romanizado: Sagwae) consta de 4 estrelas diante do *Pozo* e da *Machada de "
"batalla*."

#. Description of Korean constellation Seat Flags
msgid ""
"*Seat Flags* (Korean: 좌기, Hanja: 坐旗, Romanization: Jwagi) consists of 9 "
"stars northeast of the *Deity in Charge of Monsters*."
msgstr ""
"As *Bandeiras de asento* (en coreano: 좌기, en hanja: 坐旗, romanizado: Jwagi) "
"constan de 9 estrelas ó nordeste da *Deidade Encargada dos Monstros*."

#. Description of Korean constellation Three Stars
msgid ""
"*Three Stars* (Korean: 삼, Hanja: 參, Romanization: Sam) consists of 7 stars."
msgstr ""
"*Tres estrelas* (en coreano: 삼, en hanja: 參, romanizado: Sam) consta de 7 "
"estrelas."

#. Description of Korean constellation Send Armed Forces To Suppress (Vassal
#. of Three Stars)
msgid ""
"*Send Armed Forces To Suppress* (Korean: 벌, Hanja: 伐, Romanization: Beol) "
"consists of 3 small stars in the center of the *Three Stars*."
msgstr ""
"*Envío de Forzas Armadas para Reprimir* (coreano: 벌, hanja: 伐, romanizado: "
"Beol) consta de 3 pequenas estrelas no centro das *Tres estrelas*."

#. Description of Korean constellation Jade Well
msgid ""
"*Jade Well* (Korean: 옥정, Hanja: 玉井, Romanization: Okjeong) consists of 4 "
"stars under the left foot of the *Three Stars* (β Ori)."
msgstr ""
"O *Pozo de xade* (en coreano: 옥정, en hanja: 玉井, romanizado: Okjeong) consta "
"de 4 estrelas baixo o pé esquerdo das *Tres estrelas* (β Ori)."

#. Description of Korean constellation Military Well
msgid ""
"*Military Well* (Korean: 군정, Hanja: 軍井, Romanization: Gunjeong) consists of "
"4 stars southeast of the *Jade Well*."
msgstr ""
"O *Pozo Militar* (en coreano: 군정, en hanja: 軍井, romanizado: Gunjeong) consta"
" de 4 estrelas ó sueste do *Pozo de Xade*."

#. Description of Korean constellation Screen
msgid ""
"*Screen* (Korean: 병, Hanja: 屏, Romanization: Byeong) consists of 2 stars "
"south of the *Jade Well*."
msgstr ""
"*Pantalla* (en coreano: 병, en hanja: 屏, romanizado: Byeong) consta de 2 "
"estrelas ó sur do *Pozo de Xade*."

#. Description of Korean constellation Toilet
msgid ""
"*Toilet* (Korean: 측, Hanja: 廁, Romanization: Cheuk) consists of 4 stars east"
" of the *Screen*."
msgstr ""
"*Aseo* (coreano: 측, hanja: 廁, romanizado: Cheuk) consta de 4 estrelas ó "
"leste da *Pantalla*."

#. Description of Korean constellation Celestial Excrement
msgid ""
"*Excrement* (Korean: 천시, Hanja: 天矢, Romanization: Cheonsi) is 1 star south "
"of the *Toilet*."
msgstr ""
"*Excrementos* (en coreano: 천시, en hanja: 天矢, romanizado: Cheonsi) está a 1 "
"estrela ósur do *Aseo*."

#. Description of Korean constellation East Well
msgid ""
"*Well* (Korean: 동정, Hanja: 東井, Romanization: Dongjeong) or *Eastern Well*, "
"consists of 8 stars."
msgstr ""
"*Pozo* (en coreano: 동정, en hanja: 東井, romanizado: Dongjeong) ou *Pozo "
"Oriental*, consta de 8 estrelas."

#. Description of Korean constellation Battle Axe (Vassal of Well)
msgid ""
"*Battle Axe* (Korean: 월, Hanja: 鉞, Romanization: Wol) is 1 star attached to "
"the front of the *Well Mansion*."
msgstr ""
"*Machada de batalla* (en coreano: 월, en hanja: 鉞, romanizado: Wol) é unha "
"estrela situada na parte dianteira da *Mansión do Pozo*."

#. Description of Korean constellation Celestial Wine Cup
msgid ""
"*Celestial Wine Cup* (Korean: 천준, Hanja: 天樽, Romanization: Cheonjun) "
"consists of 3 stars north of the *Well*, south of the *Five Feudal Kings*."
msgstr ""
"A *Copa de Viño Celestial* (en coreano: 천준, en hanja: 天樽, romanizado: "
"Cheonjun) consta de 3 estrelas ó norte do *Pozo* e ó sur dos *Cinco Reis "
"Feudais*."

#. Description of Korean constellation Five Feudal Kings (In Well Mansion)
msgid ""
"*Five Feudal Kings* (Korean: 오제후, Hanja: 五諸侯, Romanization: Ojehu) consists "
"of 5 stars north of the *Eastern Well*, near the *North River*."
msgstr ""
"Os *Cinco Reis Feudais* (en coreano: 오제후, en hanja: 五諸侯, romanizado: Ojehu) "
"constan de 5 estrelas ónorte do *Pozo Oriental*, preto do *Río Norte*."

#. Description of Korean constellation North River
msgid ""
"*North River* (Korean: 북하, Hanja: 北河, Romanization: Bukha) consists of 3 "
"stars."
msgstr ""
"*Río Norte* (en coreano: 북하, en hanja: 北河, romanizado: Bukha) ten 3 "
"estrelas."

#. Description of Korean constellation South River
msgid ""
"*South River* (Korean: 남하, Hanja: 南河, Romanization: Namha) consists of 3 "
"stars northeast of the *Three Stars*."
msgstr ""
"*Río Sur* (en coreano: 남하, en hanja: 南河, romanizado: Namha) consta de 3 "
"estrelas ó  nordeste das *Tres Estrelas*."

#. Description of Korean constellation Accumulated Water (In Well Mansion)
msgid ""
"*Accumulated water* (Korean: 적수, Hanja: 積水, Romanization: Jeoksu) is 1 star "
"northwest of the *North River*."
msgstr ""
"*Auga acumulada* (en coreano: 적수, en hanja: 積水, romanizado: Jeoksu) está "
"situada a 1 estrela ó noroeste do *Río Norte*."

#. Description of Korean constellation Pile of Firewood
msgid ""
"*Pile of Firewood* (Korean: 적신, Hanja: 積薪, Romanization: Jeoksin) is 1 star "
"southeast of the *Accumulated Water*."
msgstr ""
"*Morea de leña* (coreano: 적신, hanja: 積薪, romanizado: Jeoksin) está a 1 "
"estrela ó sueste da *Auga Acumulada*."

#. Description of Korean constellation Water Level
msgid ""
"*Water Level* (Korean: 수위, Hanja: 水位, Romanization: Suwi) consists of 4 "
"stars, lined north-south east of the *Eastern Well*."
msgstr ""
"O *Nivel da auga* (en coreano: 수위, en hanja: 水位, romanizado: Suwi) consta de"
" 4 estrelas, aliñadas de norte a sureste do *Pozo oriental*."

#. Description of Korean constellation Four Channels
msgid ""
"*Four Channels* (Korean: 사독, Hanja: 四瀆, Romanization: Sadok) consists of 4 "
"stars east of the southern lined four stars of the *Eastern Well*."
msgstr ""
"*Catro Canles* (en coreano: 사독, en hanja: 四瀆, romanizado: Sadok) consta de 4"
" estrelas ó leste das catro estrelas aliñadas no sur do *Pozo Oriental*."

#. Description of Korean constellation Official for Irrigation
msgid ""
"*Official for Irrigation* (Korean: 수부, Hanja: 水府, Romanization: Subu) "
"consists of 4 stars southwest of the *Eastern Well*."
msgstr ""
"*Oficial para o Rego* (coreano: 수부, hanja: 水府, romanizado: Subu) consta de 4"
" estrelas ó suroeste do *Pozo Oriental*."

#. Description of Korean constellation Palace Gate
msgid ""
"*Palace Gate* (Korean: 궐구, Hanja: 闕丘, Romanization: Gwolgu) consists of 2 "
"stars south of the *South River*."
msgstr ""
"A *Porta do Palacio* (en coreano: 궐구, en hanja: 闕丘, romanizado: Gwolgu) "
"consta de 2 estrelas ó sur do *Río Sur*."

#. Description of Korean constellation Market for Soldiers
msgid ""
"*Market for Soldiers* (Korean: 군시, Hanja: 軍市, Romanization: Gunsi) consists "
"of 13 stars southeast of the *Three Stars*."
msgstr ""
"*Mercado para soldados* (en coreano: 군시, en hanja: 軍市, en romanización: "
"Gunsi) consta de 13 estrelas ó sueste das *Tres estrelas*."

#. Description of Korean constellation Wild Cockerel
msgid ""
"*Wild Cockerel* (Korean: 야계, Hanja: 野雞, Romanization: Yagye) is 1 star in "
"the *Market for Soldiers*."
msgstr ""
"*Galo Salvaxe* (en coreano: 야계, en hanja: 野雞, romanizado: Yagye) ten 1 "
"estrela no *Mercado para soldados*."

#. Description of Korean constellation Wolf Star
msgid ""
"*Wolf* (Korean: 낭성, Hanja: 狼星, Romanization: Nangseong) or *Celestial Wolf* "
"is 1 star southeast of the *Three Stars*."
msgstr ""
"*Lobo* (coreano: 낭성, Hanja: 狼星, romanizado: Nangseong) ou *Lobo Celestial* é"
" 1 estrela ó sueste das *Tres Estrelas*."

#. Description of Korean constellation Bow
msgid ""
"*Bow and Arrow* (Korean: 호, Hanja: 弧, Romanization: Ho) consists of 9 stars "
"southeast of the *Wolf*."
msgstr ""
"*Arco e Frecha* (en coreano: 호, en hanja: 弧, romanizado: Ho) consta de 9 "
"estrelas ó sueste do *Lobo*."

#. Description of Korean constellation Grandfather
msgid ""
"*Grandfather* (Korean: 장인, Hanja: 丈人, Romanization: Jangin) consists of 2 "
"stars southwest of the *Market for Soldiers*."
msgstr ""
"*Avó* (coreano: 장인, hanja: 丈人, romanizado: Jangin) consta de 2 estrelas ó "
"suroeste do *Mercado para Soldados*."

#. Description of Korean constellation Son
msgid ""
"*Son* (Korean: 자, Hanja: 子, Romanization: Ja) consists of 2 stars east of "
"the *Grandfather*."
msgstr ""
"*Fillo* (coreano: 자, hanja: 子, romanizado: Ja) consta de 2 estrelas ó leste "
"do *Avó*."

#. Description of Korean constellation Grandson
msgid ""
"*Grandson* (Korean: 손, Hanja: 孫, Romanization: Son) consists of 2 stars east"
" of the *Son*."
msgstr ""
"*Neto* (en coreano: 손, en hanja: 孫, romanizado: Son) consta de 2 estrelas ó "
"leste de *Fillo*."

#. Description of Korean constellation Old Man
msgid ""
"*Old Man* (Korean: 노인, Hanja: 老人, Romanization: Noin) is 1 star south of the"
" *Bow and Arrow*."
msgstr ""
"*Home Vello* (coreano: 노인, hanja: 老人, romanizado: Noin) está 1 estrela ó sur"
" do *Arco e Frecha*."

#. Description of Korean constellation Ghosts
msgid "*Ghosts* (Korean: 귀, Hanja: 鬼, Romanization: Gwi) consists of 4 stars."
msgstr ""
"*Pantasmas* (en coreano: 귀, en hanja: 鬼, romanizado: Gwi) ten 4 estrelas."

#. Description of Korean constellation Cumulative Corpse Gas (In Ghosts
#. Mansion)
msgid ""
"*Cumulative Corpse Gas* (Korean: 적시, Hanja: 積尸, Romanization: Jeoksi) is 1 "
"star in the center of the *Ghosts Mansion*."
msgstr ""
"*Gas Acumulado de Cadáveres* (en coreano: 적시, en hanja: 積尸, romanizado: "
"Jeoksi) é un lugar de 1 estrela situado no centro da *Mansión das "
"Pantasmas*."

#. Description of Korean constellation Beacon Fire
msgid ""
"*Beacon Fire* (Korean: 관, Hanja: 爟, Romanization: Gwan) consists of 4 stars "
"west of the tail of *Xuanyuan*, northwest of the *Ghosts*."
msgstr ""
"*Faro de Lume* (coreano: 관, hanja: 爟, romanizado: Gwan) consta de 4 estrelas"
" ó oeste do rabo de *Xuanyuan*, ó noroeste das *Pantasmas*."

#. Description of Korean constellation Outer Kitchen
msgid ""
"*Outer Kitchen* (Korean: 외주, Hanja: 外厨, Romanization: Oeju) consists of 6 "
"stars south of the *Willow*."
msgstr ""
"*Cociña Exterior* (en coreano: 외주, en hanja: 外厨, romanizado: Oeju) consta de"
" 6 estrelas ó sur do *Salgueiro*."

#. Description of Korean constellation Celestial Dog
msgid ""
"*Celestial Dog* (Korean: 천구, Hanja: 天狗, Romanization: Cheongu) consists of 7"
" stars northeast of the *Wolf*."
msgstr ""
"*Can Celestial* (en coreano: 천구, en hanja: 天狗, romanizado: Cheongu) consta "
"de 7 estrelas ó nordeste do *Lobo*."

#. Description of Korean constellation Celestial Earth God's Temple
msgid ""
"*Celestial Earth God's Temple* (Korean: 천사, Hanja: 天社, Romanization: "
"Cheonsa) consists of 6 stars south of the *Bow and Arrow*."
msgstr ""
"O *Templo do Deus Celestial da Terra* (en coreano: 천사, en hanja: 天社, "
"romanizado: Cheonsa) consta de 6 estrelas ó sur do *Arco e Frecha*."

#. Description of Korean constellation Willow
msgid "*Willow* (Korean: 유, Hanja: 柳, Romanization: Yu) consists of 8 stars."
msgstr ""
"*Salgueiro* (en coreano: 유, en hanja: 柳, romanizado: Yu) ten 8 estrelas."

#. Description of Korean constellation Banner of Wine Shop
msgid ""
"*Banner of Wine Shop* (Korean: 주기, Hanja: 酒旗, Romanization: Jugi) consists "
"of 3 stars south of the right tip of *Xuanyuan*."
msgstr ""
"O *Estandarte da Tenda de Viños* (en coreano: 주기, en hanja: 酒旗, romanizado "
"Jugi) consta de 3 estrelas ó sur do extremo dereito de *Xuanyuan*."

#. Description of Korean constellation Star
msgid "*Star* (Korean: 성, Hanja: 星, Romanization: Seong) consists of 7 stars."
msgstr ""
"*Estrela* (coreano: 성, hanja: 星, romanizado: Seong) consta de 7 estrelas."

#. Description of Korean constellation Xuanyuan
msgid ""
"*Xuanyuan* (Korean: 헌원, Hanja: 軒轅, Romanization: Heon-won) consists of 17 "
"stars north of the *Star mansion*."
msgstr ""
"*Xuanyuan* (en coreano: 헌원, en hanja: 軒轅, romanizado: Heon-won) consta de 17"
" estrelas ó norte da *Mansión da Estrela*."

#. Description of Korean constellation High Judge
msgid ""
"*High Judge* (Korean: 내평, Hanja: 內平, Romanization: Naepyeong) consists of 4 "
"stars south of the *Middle Step*."
msgstr ""
"O *Alto Xuíz* (en coreano: 내평, en hanja: 內平, romanizado: Naepyeong) consta "
"de 4 estrelas ó sur do *Chanzo do Medio*."

#. Description of Korean constellation Celestial Premier
msgid ""
"*Celestial Premier* (Korean: 천상, Hanja: 天相, Romanization: Cheonsang) "
"consists of 3 stars east of the *Star mansion*, south of the *Banner of Wine"
" Shop*."
msgstr ""
"*Pdrimeiro Ministro Celestial* (en coreano: 천상, en hanja: 天相, romanizado: "
"Cheonsang) consta de 3 estrelas ó leste da *Mansión da Estrela* e ó sur do "
"Estandarte da Tenda de Viños*."

#. Description of Korean constellation Cereals
msgid ""
"*Celestial Cereals* (Korean: 직, Hanja: 稷, Romanization: Jik) consists of 5 "
"stars south of the *Star mansion*."
msgstr ""
"*Cereais Celestiais* (en coreano: 직, en hanja: 稷, romanizado: Jik) constan "
"de 5 estrelas ó sur da *Mansión da Estrela*."

#. Description of Korean constellation Extended Net
msgid ""
"*Extended Net* (Korean: 장, Hanja: 張, Romanization: Jang) consists of 6 "
"stars."
msgstr ""
"*Rede Estendida* (en coreano: 장, en hanja: 張, romanizado: Jang) consta de 6 "
"estrelas."

#. Description of Korean constellation Celestial Temple
msgid ""
"*Celestial Temple* (Korean: 천묘, Hanja: 天廟, Romanization: Cheonmyo) consists "
"of 14 stars south of the *Extended Net*."
msgstr ""
"O *Templo Celestial* (en coreano: 천묘, en hanja: 天廟, romanizado: Cheonmyo) "
"consta de 14 estrelas ó sur da *Rede Estendida*."

#. Description of Korean constellation Wings
msgid "*Wings* (Korean: 익, Hanja: 翼, Romanization: Ik) consists of 22 stars."
msgstr "*Ás* (coreano: 익, Hanja: 翼, romanizado: Ik) consta de 22 estrelas."

#. Description of Korean constellation Dongou
msgid ""
"*Dong'ou* (Korean: 동구, Hanja: 東甌, Romanization: Donggu) consists of 5 stars "
"south of the Wings."
msgstr ""
"*Dong'ou* (en coreano: 동구, en hanja: 東甌, romanizado: Donggu) consta de 5 "
"estrelas ó sur das ás."

#. Description of Korean constellation Chariot
msgid ""
"*Chariot* (Korean: 진, Hanja: 軫, Romanization: Jin) consists of 4 stars."
msgstr ""
"*Carro* (en coreano: 진, en hanja: 軫, romanizadfo: Jin) consta de 4 estrelas."

#. Description of Korean constellation Left linchpin (Vassal of Chariot)
msgid ""
"*Left linchpin* (Korean: 좌할, Hanja: 左轄, Romanization: Jwahal) consists of 1 "
"star."
msgstr ""
"*Eixo Esquerdo* (en coreano: 좌할, en hanja: 左轄, romanizado: Jwahal) consta "
"dunha estrela."

#. Description of Korean constellation Right linchpin (Vassal of Chariot)
msgid ""
"*Right linchpin* (Korean: 우할, Hanja: 右轄, Romanization: Uhal) consists of 1 "
"star."
msgstr ""
"*Eixe Dereito* (coreano: 우할, Hanja: 右轄, romanizado: Uhal) consta dunha "
"estrela."

#. Description of Korean constellation Changsha (Vassal of Chariot)
msgid ""
"*Changsha* (Korean: 장사, Hanja: 長沙, Romanization: Jangsa) is 1 star in the "
"*Chariot Mansion*."
msgstr ""
"*Changsha* (coreano: 장사, Hanja: 長沙, romanizado: Jangsa) é 1 estrela na "
"*Mansión do Carro*."

#. Description of Korean constellation Military Gate
msgid ""
"*Military Gate* (Korean: 군문, Hanja: 軍門, Romanization: Gunmun) consists of 2 "
"stars west of the *Green Hill*, north of the *Master of Constructions*."
msgstr ""
"A *Porta Militar* (en coreano: 군문, en hanja: 軍門, romanizado: Gunmun) consta "
"de 2 estrelas ó oeste do *Outeiro Verde*, ó norte do *Mestre das "
"Construcións*."

#. Description of Korean constellation Master of Constructions (In Chariot
#. Mansion)
msgid ""
"*Master of Constructions* (Korean: 토사공, Hanja: 土司空, Romanization: Tosagong) "
"consists of 4 stars south of the *Military Gate*, west of the *Green Hill*."
msgstr ""
"*Mestre das Construcións* (en coreano: 토사공, en hanja: 土司空, romanizado: "
"Tosagong) consta de 4 estrelas ó sur da *Porta Militar*, ó oeste do *Outeiro"
" Verde*."

#. Description of Korean constellation Green Hill
msgid ""
"*Green Hill* (Korean: 청구, Hanja: 青丘, Romanization: Cheonggu) consists of 7 "
"stars southeast of the *Chariot*."
msgstr ""
"*Outeiro Verde* (en coreano: 청구, en hanja: 青丘, romanizado: Cheonggu) consta "
"de 7 estrelas ó sueste do *Carro*."

#. Description of Korean constellation House for Musical Instruments
msgid ""
"*House for Musical Instruments* (Korean: 기부, Hanja: 器府, Romanization: Gibu) "
"consists of 32 stars south of the *Chariot*."
msgstr ""
"A *Casa dos Instrumentos Musicais* (en coreano: 기부, en hanja: 器府, "
"romanizado: Gibu) consta de 32 estrelas ó sur do *Carro*."

